Justin Randall Timberlake (born January 31, 1981) [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-grammy-1]  is an American singer, songwriter, actor, record producer, and dancer. [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-2]  Dubbed the " [LINK: (Prince of Pop) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honorific_nicknames_in_popular_music] ", he is an influential figure in  [LINK: (popular music) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Popular_music] . Timberlake is one of the  [LINK: (best-selling music artists) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_best-selling_music_artists]  of all time, with estimated sales of 88 million records worldwide. [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-3]

Born and raised in  [LINK: (Memphis, Tennessee) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memphis,_Tennessee] , Timberlake appeared on musical television shows as a child, competing on  [LINK: (Star Search) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_Search] ; in the early to mid-1990s, he was a cast member on the  [LINK: (Disney Channel) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disney_Channel] 's  [LINK: (The All New Mickey Mouse Club) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mickey_Mouse_Club#1989–94_revival:_The_All-New_Mickey_Mouse_Club] , where he performed cover songs, skits, and choreography. On the show, Timberlake met and worked with future bandmate  [LINK: (JC Chasez) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JC_Chasez] , and the two later rose to prominence as the  [LINK: (lead vocalists) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lead_vocalist]  of the  [LINK: (pop) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pop_music]   [LINK: (boy band) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boy_band]   [LINK: (NSYNC) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NSYNC] . The group released four commercially successful studio albums, becoming one of the  [LINK: (best-selling) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Best-selling]  boy bands of all time with sales of over 70 million units worldwide.

Timberlake established himself as a solo artist with his first two albums,  [LINK: (Justified) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justified_(album)]  (2002) and  [LINK: (FutureSex/LoveSounds) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FutureSex/LoveSounds]  (2006), both of which sold over 10 million copies and received  [LINK: (triple platinum) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RIAA_certification]  certifications by the  [LINK: (RIAA) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RIAA] , with the latter became his first to debut atop the US  [LINK: (Billboard 200) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_200] . His next three albums also peaked the chart as well:  [LINK: (The 20/20 Experience) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_20/20_Experience] ,  [LINK: (The 20/20 Experience – 2 of 2) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_20/20_Experience_%E2%80%93_2_of_2]  (both 2013) and  [LINK: (Man of the Woods) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Man_of_the_Woods]  (2018); the former became the  [LINK: (best-selling album of the year) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_best-selling_albums_by_year_in_the_United_States] . Throughout his career, Timberlake scored numerous high-charting US  [LINK: (Billboard Hot 100) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Hot_100]  singles, including " [LINK: (Cry Me a River) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cry_Me_a_River_(Justin_Timberlake_song)] ", " [LINK: (Rock Your Body) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_Your_Body] ", " [LINK: (SexyBack) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SexyBack] ", " [LINK: (My Love) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/My_Love_(Justin_Timberlake_song)] ", " [LINK: (LoveStoned/I Think She Knows) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LoveStoned] ", " [LINK: (What Goes Around... Comes Around) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/What_Goes_Around..._Comes_Around] ", " [LINK: (Give It to Me) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Give_It_to_Me_(Timbaland_song)] ", " [LINK: (4 Minutes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/4_Minutes] ", " [LINK: (Pusher Love Girl) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pusher_Love_Girl] ", " [LINK: (Suit & Tie) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suit_%26_Tie] ", " [LINK: (Mirrors) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirrors_(Justin_Timberlake_song)] " and " [LINK: (Can't Stop the Feeling!) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Can%27t_Stop_the_Feeling!] ", which earned him an  [LINK: (Academy Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Academy_Award_for_Best_Original_Song]  nomination.

Timberlake enhanced his popularity with  [LINK: (an acting career) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake_videography] . He landed starring roles in the films  [LINK: (The Love Guru) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Love_Guru]  (2008),  [LINK: (The Social Network) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Social_Network]  (2010),  [LINK: (Bad Teacher) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bad_Teacher]  (2011),  [LINK: (Friends with Benefits) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friends_with_Benefits_(film)]  (2011),  [LINK: (In Time) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_Time]  (2011),  [LINK: (Wonder Wheel) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wonder_Wheel_(film)]  (2017) and  [LINK: (Palmer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palmer_(film)]  (2021). He also  [LINK: (voiced) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voice_acting]   [LINK: (Artie) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_Arthur]  in  [LINK: (Shrek the Third) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shrek_the_Third]  (2007),  [LINK: (Boo-Boo Bear) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boo-Boo_Bear]  in  [LINK: (Yogi Bear) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yogi_Bear_(film)]  (2010) and Branch in the  [LINK: (Trolls franchise) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trolls_(franchise)]  since 2016.  [LINK: (Billboard) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_(magazine)]  named him one of the  [LINK: (greatest pop stars of the 21st century) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard%27s_Greatest_Pop_Stars_of_the_21st_Century] . [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-4]  [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-5]  His  [LINK: (awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_awards_and_nominations_received_by_Justin_Timberlake]  include ten  [LINK: (Grammy Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammy_Awards] , four  [LINK: (Primetime Emmy Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primetime_Emmy_Awards] , three  [LINK: (Brit Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brit_Awards] , nine  [LINK: (Billboard Music Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Music_Awards] , the  [LINK: (Contemporary Icon Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Songwriters_Hall_of_Fame#Contemporary_Icon_Award]  by the  [LINK: (Songwriters Hall of Fame) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Songwriters_Hall_of_Fame] , and  [LINK: (MTV) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MTV] 's  [LINK: (Michael Jackson Video Vanguard Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Jackson_Video_Vanguard_Award] . He has frequently collaborated with producers such as  [LINK: (The Neptunes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Neptunes]  and  [LINK: (Timbaland) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timbaland] , who are best known for boosting Timberlake's solo career.


# EARLY LIFE #

Justin Randall Timberlake was born on January 31, 1981, in  [LINK: (Memphis, Tennessee) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memphis,_Tennessee] , [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-grammy-1]  the son of Janet Lynn (née Bomar) Harless and Charles Randall Timberlake, a  [LINK: (Baptist) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baptist]  church choir director. [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-6]  [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-7]  [LINK: ([8]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-8]  [LINK: ([9]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-9]  Timberlake has two half-brothers, Jonathan and Stephen, from Charles' second marriage to Lisa Perry. His half-sister Laura Katherine died shortly after birth in 1997, and is mentioned in his acknowledgments in the album  [LINK: (NSYNC) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NSYNC_(album)]  as "My Angel in Heaven".

His family circle includes several musicians; [LINK: ([10]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-10]  his grandfather introduced him to music from  [LINK: (country music) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Country_music]  artists like  [LINK: (Johnny Cash) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johnny_Cash]  and  [LINK: (Willie Nelson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willie_Nelson] . [LINK: ([11]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-rsinterview-11]  Performing as a child, Timberlake sang country and  [LINK: (gospel music) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gospel_music] : at the age of 11, he appeared on the television show  [LINK: (Star Search) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_Search] , performing country songs as "Justin Randall". [LINK: ([12]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-12]  By that time, he began listening to  [LINK: (rhythm and blues) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhythm_and_blues]  musicians from the 1960s and 70s, such as  [LINK: (Al Green) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Green] ,  [LINK: (Stevie Wonder) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stevie_Wonder]  and  [LINK: (Marvin Gaye) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marvin_Gaye] , and he had listening sessions with his father of studio albums by the  [LINK: (Eagles) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagles_(band)]  and  [LINK: (Bob Seger) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bob_Seger] . [LINK: ([11]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-rsinterview-11]

From 1993 to 1995, he was a Mouseketeer on  [LINK: (The All New Mickey Mouse Club) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mickey_Mouse_Club#1989–1994_revival:_The_All-New_Mickey_Mouse_Club] , where his castmates included future girlfriend and singer  [LINK: (Britney Spears) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Britney_Spears] , future tourmate  [LINK: (Christina Aguilera) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christina_Aguilera] , future bandmate  [LINK: (JC Chasez) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JC_Chasez] , and future actors  [LINK: (Ryan Gosling) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryan_Gosling]  and  [LINK: (Keri Russell) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keri_Russell] . [LINK: ([13]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-allmusicbio-13]  In 1995, Timberlake recruited Chasez to be in an all-male singing group, put together by  [LINK: (Chris Kirkpatrick) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Kirkpatrick]  and financed by boy band manager  [LINK: (Lou Pearlman) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lou_Pearlman] , that eventually became  [LINK: (NSYNC) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NSYNC] . [LINK: ([14]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-14]


# CAREER #

The  [LINK: (boy band) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boy_band]   [LINK: (NSYNC) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NSYNC]  formed in 1995, and they began recording and performing in 1996 in Europe; Timberlake and Chasez served as its two lead singers. [LINK: ([15]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-15]  In 1998, the group rose to prominence in the United States with the release of their  [LINK: (self-titled debut studio album) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NSYNC_(album)] , which sold 11 million copies [LINK: ([16]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-16]  and includes the single " [LINK: (Tearin' Up My Heart) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tearin%27_Up_My_Heart] ". [LINK: ([17]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-USRadio-17]  The group had a series of legal battles with former manager  [LINK: (Lou Pearlman) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lou_Pearlman] , [LINK: ([18]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-Pearlman1-18]  and they subsequently signed with  [LINK: (Jive Records) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jive_Records] . [LINK: ([19]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-19]  They released their third studio album  [LINK: (No Strings Attached) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/No_Strings_Attached_(NSYNC_album)]  (2000), which sold 2.4 million copies in the first week, becoming the fastest-selling album of all time. [LINK: ([20]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-20]  They held this record until 2015 when  [LINK: (Adele) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adele]  surpassed the record with her third album  [LINK: (25) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/25_(Adele_album)] . [LINK: ([21]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-21]   [LINK: (No Strings Attached) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/No_Strings_Attached_(NSYNC_album)]  also includes the number one single " [LINK: (It's Gonna Be Me) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/It%27s_Gonna_Be_Me] ", [LINK: ([22]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-22]  " [LINK: (Bye Bye Bye) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bye_Bye_Bye] ", [LINK: ([23]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-usrel-23]  and " [LINK: (This I Promise You) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/This_I_Promise_You] ". [LINK: ([24]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-ET20-24]  The same year, Timberlake made his film debut in  [LINK: (The Wonderful World of Disney) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Wonderful_World_of_Disney]  film  [LINK: (Model Behavior) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Model_Behavior] . He played Jason Sharpe, a model who falls in love with a waitress after mistaking her for another model. [LINK: ([25]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-25]  He also appeared as a young  [LINK: (Elton John) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elton_John] , in the video for John's song " [LINK: (This Train Don't Stop There Anymore) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/This_Train_Don%27t_Stop_There_Anymore] ", the following year. [LINK: ([26]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-26]  NSYNC's fourth studio album  [LINK: (Celebrity) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celebrity_(album)]  (2001) was also financially successful, selling 1.8 million copies in the first week [LINK: ([27]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-27]  and spawning the top-five single " [LINK: (Girlfriend) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girlfriend_(NSYNC_song)] ". [LINK: ([28]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-baker-28]  Upon the completion of the  [LINK: (Celebrity Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celebrity_Tour] , the group went on an indefinite hiatus in 2002. [LINK: ([29]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-29]  NSYNC performed at the  [LINK: (Academy Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Academy_Awards]  in 2000, [LINK: ([30]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-30]  the  [LINK: (2002 Winter Olympics) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2002_Winter_Olympics] , [LINK: ([31]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-31]  and the  [LINK: (Super Bowl XXXV halftime show) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Bowl_XXXV_halftime_show] . [LINK: ([32]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-32]  The band sold more than 70 million records worldwide, becoming the  [LINK: (fifth-best selling boy band) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boy_band#top]  in history. [LINK: ([33]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-nsync_records-33]

The rise of Timberlake's own stardom and the general decline in the popularity of boy bands led to the dissolution of NSYNC. Band member  [LINK: (Lance Bass) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lance_Bass]  was openly critical of Timberlake's actions in his memoir  [LINK: (Out of Sync) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Out_of_Sync_(book)] . [LINK: ([34]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-34]  By 2002, when the group went on an indefinite hiatus and members were doing individual projects, he partnered with  [LINK: (Pharrell Williams) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pharrell_Williams]  of the producing team  [LINK: (The Neptunes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Neptunes] –and  [LINK: (Timbaland) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timbaland]  to start working on new music. [LINK: ([35]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-vanity_fair-35]  The idea of going solo was strengthened a year earlier. Timberlake originally wrote the single " [LINK: (Gone) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gone_(NSYNC_song)] " around 2001 for  [LINK: (Michael Jackson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Jackson] , but he turned the song down, and it was instead recorded by NSYNC. Before its release, however, Jackson contacted him. Timberlake declared in a later interview that the first time he felt confident to go solo happened after that conversation. [LINK: ([36]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-jackson-36]  In a retrospective article in 2020,  [LINK: (Billboard) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_(magazine)]  considered Celebrity "the group's swan song, setting the stage for Timberlake's equally massive solo career". [LINK: ([37]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-Greatest-37]

[Michael] called me on the phone and said that he wanted to cut the record ("Gone"), but he wanted it to be a duet between himself and I. And I said, 'Well ... we've already cut the song as an 'N Sync record. Could we do, like, 'N Sync featuring Michael Jackson', or 'Michael Jackson featuring 'N Sync'? And he was very absolute about the fact that he wanted it to be a duet between himself and I.. [That was] the first time I ever really felt the confidence to do it

In August 2002, Timberlake performed at the  [LINK: (2002 MTV Video Music Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2002_MTV_Video_Music_Awards] , where he premiered his debut solo single " [LINK: (Like I Love You) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Like_I_Love_You] "; [LINK: ([38]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-38]  it peaked at number 11 on the  [LINK: (Billboard Hot 100) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Hot_100]  [LINK: ([39]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-timberlake_billboard-39]  and number two on the  [LINK: (UK Singles Chart) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UK_Singles_Chart] . [LINK: ([40]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-40]  His debut solo studio album  [LINK: (Justified) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justified_(album)]  was released in November [LINK: ([41]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-41]  and debuted at number two on the  [LINK: (Billboard 200) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_200]  with first-week sales of 439,000 copies, [LINK: ([42]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-mtv4-42]  fewer than previous 'N Sync releases. It sold over three million copies in the U.S. and more than ten million copies worldwide. [LINK: ([43]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-43]  Its  [LINK: (R&B) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contemporary_R%26B]  influence, provided by  [LINK: (hip-hop) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hip-hop]  producers  [LINK: (The Neptunes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Neptunes]  and  [LINK: (Timbaland) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timbaland] , [LINK: ([44]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-44]  was complimented by music critics. About the musical direction of the record, he commented, "I just want to do R&B. It's what I grew up listening to". [LINK: ([45]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-45]  The album spawned the top-five singles " [LINK: (Cry Me a River) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cry_Me_a_River_(Justin_Timberlake_song)] " and " [LINK: (Rock Your Body) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_Your_Body] ". [LINK: ([39]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-timberlake_billboard-39]

Near the end of 2002, Timberlake was the first celebrity to appear on  [LINK: (Punk'd) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Punk%27d] , a "candid camera" type show created by  [LINK: (Ashton Kutcher) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashton_Kutcher]  to trick celebrities. [LINK: ([46]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-46]  Timberlake, who cried during the episode, later admitted to being under the influence of  [LINK: (cannabis) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cannabis_(drug)]  when he was pranked. [LINK: ([47]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-47]  Three episodes later, he set up  [LINK: (Kelly Osbourne) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kelly_Osbourne]  to be "punk'd", thus making him the first celebrity to appear on the show more than once. [LINK: ([48]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-48]  Timberlake later spoofed  [LINK: (Ashton Kutcher) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashton_Kutcher]  and Punk'd in a 2003 episode of NBC's  [LINK: (Saturday Night Live) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saturday_Night_Live] . [LINK: ([49]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-49]  Timberlake co-starred in a skit titled  [LINK: (The Barry Gibb Talk Show) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Barry_Gibb_Talk_Show]  alongside comedian  [LINK: (Jimmy Fallon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jimmy_Fallon] , where the duo portrayed  [LINK: (Bee Gees) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bee_Gees]  brothers  [LINK: (Barry) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barry_Gibb]  and  [LINK: (Robin Gibb) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robin_Gibb] . It marked the beginning of a long-running friendship and collaboration with Fallon. [LINK: ([50]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-jfallon-50]

In summer 2003, Timberlake and  [LINK: (Christina Aguilera) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christina_Aguilera]  co-headlined  [LINK: (The Justified & Stripped Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Justified_%26_Stripped_Tour] . [LINK: ([51]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-51]  Later that year, he released the single " [LINK: (I'm Lovin' It) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I%27m_Lovin%27_It_(song)] ", used by  [LINK: (McDonald's) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McDonald%27s]  as the theme to its "I'm Lovin' It" campaign. The deal with McDonald's earned Timberlake an estimated $6 million. [LINK: ([52]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-p4k-52]  A tour titled  [LINK: (Justified and Lovin' It Live) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justified_and_Lovin%27_It_Live]  was included with the deal, following his initial  [LINK: (Justified World Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justified_World_Tour] . [LINK: ([53]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-53]  Timberlake was featured on  [LINK: (Nelly) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nelly] 's song, " [LINK: (Work It) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Work_It_(Nelly_song)] ", which was  [LINK: (remixed) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Remix]  and included on Nelly's 2003 remix album. [LINK: ([54]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-54]  In October 2003, Timberlake made his first sole appearance on  [LINK: (Saturday Night Live) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saturday_Night_Live]  both as host and music guest, pairing with comedian  [LINK: (Jimmy Fallon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jimmy_Fallon]  on the later-recurring skit  [LINK: (The Barry Gibb Talk Show) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Barry_Gibb_Talk_Show] . [LINK: ([55]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-revs_up-55]  [LINK: ([56]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-Moss-56]

In February 2004, during the  [LINK: (Super Bowl XXXVIII halftime show) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Bowl_XXXVIII_halftime_show] , broadcast on the  [LINK: (CBS) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CBS]  television network from  [LINK: (Houston) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Houston] , Timberlake performed with  [LINK: (Janet Jackson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janet_Jackson]  before a television audience of more than 140 million viewers. At the end of the performance, as the song drew to a close, Timberlake tore off a part of Jackson's black leather costume in a "costume reveal" meant to accompany a portion of the song lyrics. Jackson's representative explained Timberlake intended "to pull away the rubber bustier to reveal a red lace bra. Part of the costume detached, and Jackson's breast was briefly exposed. [LINK: ([57]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-CNNCostumeReveal-57]  Timberlake apologized for the incident, stating he was "sorry that anyone was offended by the wardrobe malfunction during the halftime performance of the Super Bowl..." [LINK: ([57]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-CNNCostumeReveal-57]  The phrase " [LINK: (wardrobe malfunction) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wardrobe_malfunction] " has since been used by the media to refer to the incident and has entered  [LINK: (pop culture) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pop_culture] . [LINK: ([58]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-58]  Timberlake and Jackson were threatened with exclusion from the  [LINK: (2004 Grammy Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2004_Grammy_Awards]  unless they agreed to apologize on screen at the event. Timberlake attended and issued a scripted apology when accepting the first of two  [LINK: (Grammy Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammy_Award]  he received that night ( [LINK: (Best Pop Vocal Album) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Best_Pop_Vocal_Album]  for Justified and  [LINK: (Best Male Pop Vocal Performance) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Best_Male_Pop_Vocal_Performance]  for "Cry Me a River"). [LINK: ([59]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-:0-59]  He had also been nominated for  [LINK: (Album of the Year) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammy_Award_for_Album_of_the_Year]  for Justified, and  [LINK: (Record of the Year) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Record_of_the_Year]  along with  [LINK: (Best Rap/Sung Collaboration) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Best_Rap/Sung_Collaboration]  for " [LINK: (Where Is the Love?) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Where_Is_the_Love%3F] " with  [LINK: (The Black Eyed Peas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Black_Eyed_Peas] . [LINK: ([59]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-:0-59]

After the Super Bowl incident, Timberlake was "burned out" from his music career, opting out of an NSYNC reunion and elevating his acting career, [LINK: ([55]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-revs_up-55]  having starred in a few feature films earlier in his career. [LINK: ([13]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-allmusicbio-13]  The first role he took during this time was as a journalist in  [LINK: (Edison Force) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edison_Force] , filmed in 2004 and released direct-to-video on July 18, 2006. [LINK: ([60]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-60]  He also appeared in the films  [LINK: (Alpha Dog) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alpha_Dog]  (2006) with  [LINK: (Bruce Willis) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruce_Willis] , [LINK: ([61]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-61]  [LINK: ([62]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-62]   [LINK: (Black Snake Moan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Snake_Moan_(film)]  (2006) with  [LINK: (Samuel L. Jackson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samuel_L._Jackson] , [LINK: ([63]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-63]  [LINK: ([64]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-64]   [LINK: (Richard Kelly) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Kelly_(director)] 's  [LINK: (Southland Tales) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southland_Tales]  (2006), [LINK: ([65]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-goodbye-65]  and voiced  [LINK: (Prince Artie Pendragon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_Arthur]  in the animated film  [LINK: (Shrek the Third) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shrek_the_Third]  (2007). [LINK: ([66]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-66]  Timberlake was considered to play the role of Roger Davis in the  [LINK: (film version) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rent_(film)]  of the rock musical  [LINK: (Rent) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rent_(musical)] , but director  [LINK: (Chris Columbus) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Columbus_(filmmaker)]  had insisted that only the original  [LINK: (Broadway) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Broadway_theatre]  members could convey the true meaning of Rent, so the role was reprised by  [LINK: (Adam Pascal) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adam_Pascal] . [LINK: ([67]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-67]

During his hiatus from music, he continued to record with other artists. In 2004, he recorded "Good Foot" with Timbaland for the  [LINK: (soundtrack) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shark_Tale#Soundtrack]  of  [LINK: (Shark Tale) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shark_Tale] . [LINK: ([68]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-janet-68]  After " [LINK: (Where Is the Love?) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Where_Is_the_Love%3F] ", he again collaborated with the Black Eyed Peas on the 2005 track "My Style" from their album  [LINK: (Monkey Business) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monkey_Business_(The_Black_Eyed_Peas_album)] . [LINK: ([69]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-69]  That year, he collaborated with  [LINK: (Charlie Wilson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlie_Wilson_(singer)]  and Black Eyed Peas member  [LINK: (Will.i.am) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Will.i.am]  on the song "Floatin'" on the former's album  [LINK: (Charlie, Last Name Wilson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlie,_Last_Name_Wilson] , [LINK: ([70]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-70]  and collaborated on a track with Brazilian music artist  [LINK: (Sérgio Mendes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%A9rgio_Mendes]  the following year. [LINK: ([71]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-71]  When recording the 2005 single " [LINK: (Signs) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Signs_(Snoop_Dogg_song)] " with  [LINK: (Snoop Dogg) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snoop_Dogg] , Timberlake discovered a throat condition. [LINK: ([72]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-72]   [LINK: (Nodules) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nodule_(medicine)]  were subsequently removed from his throat in an operation that took place on May 5, 2005. [LINK: ([73]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-73]  He was advised not to sing or speak loudly for at least a few months. [LINK: ([74]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-74]  In 2005, he began his own record company,  [LINK: (JayTee records) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JayTee_records] . [LINK: ([75]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-75]

FutureSex/LoveSounds, a full-length LP of coherence and uniform song-to-song quality virtually unheard of in pop music since the '80s golden age of Michael, Madonna, Janet and Prince... Like one of his suit-and-vest combos, Timberlake himself continued to wear pop stardom exceptionally well. He glided through his music videos and live performances with the confidence of a man who'd already spent a large percentage of his life in the spotlight, and who never doubted he'd be able to return to music on top.

In December 2005, Timberlake began production on his second studio album,  [LINK: (FutureSex/LoveSounds) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FutureSex/LoveSounds] , with returning producer Timbaland. [LINK: ([55]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-revs_up-55]  Wanting an experimental direction, his goal for the album was "to capture moments' with a vivid, raw, off-the-cuff sound", while managing the recording sessions. [LINK: ([76]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-Moss_p_2-76]  [LINK: ([77]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-Moss3-77]  At the time, Timberlake developed an interest in a  [LINK: (rock) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_music]  direction, [LINK: ([55]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-revs_up-55]  drawing inspiration from  [LINK: (David Bowie) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Bowie]  and  [LINK: (Prince) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_(musician)] , [LINK: ([78]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-backsexy-78]  and even took influence from  [LINK: (trance music) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trance_music]  into the album. [LINK: ([79]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-HovaVibeStudio-79]  In July 2006, the album's lead single, " [LINK: (SexyBack) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SexyBack] ", was released, [LINK: ([80]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-timb-80]  and by a few weeks, reached number-one on the Billboard Hot 100, where it remained for seven consecutive weeks. [LINK: ([81]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-81]

Timberlake released his second studio album,  [LINK: (FutureSex/LoveSounds) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FutureSex/LoveSounds] , on September 12, 2006. The album, which Timberlake created from 2005 to 2006, debuted at number-one on the Billboard 200 album chart, selling 684,000 copies its first week. [LINK: ([82]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-82]  It became the biggest album for pre-orders on  [LINK: (iTunes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ITunes_Store] , and beat  [LINK: (Coldplay) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coldplay] 's record for the biggest one-week sales of a digital album. [LINK: ([83]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-83]  The album was produced by Timbaland and  [LINK: (Danja) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Danja_(record_producer)]  (who produced a bulk of the album),  [LINK: (will.i.am) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Will.i.am] ,  [LINK: (Rick Rubin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rick_Rubin]  and Timberlake himself, and features guest vocals by  [LINK: (Snoop Dogg) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snoop_Dogg] ,  [LINK: (Three 6 Mafia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Three_6_Mafia] ,  [LINK: (T.I.) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T.I.]  and will.i.am. [LINK: ([84]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-84]  A studio representative described it as being "all about sexiness" and aiming for "an adult feel". [LINK: ([85]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-85]   " [LINK: (My Love) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/My_Love_(Justin_Timberlake_song)] ", the album's second single, also produced by Timbaland and featuring rapper  [LINK: (T.I.) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T.I.] , [LINK: ([86]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-norris-86]  reached number-one on the Hot 100, [LINK: ([87]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-87]  as did its third single, " [LINK: (What Goes Around... Comes Around) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/What_Goes_Around..._Comes_Around] ". [LINK: ([88]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-88]  The song is reported to have been inspired by the break-up of his childhood friend and business partner, Trace Ayala, with actress  [LINK: (Elisha Cuthbert) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elisha_Cuthbert] . [LINK: ([89]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-89]

Timberlake hosted many music events, including the  [LINK: (2006 European MTV Music Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2006_MTV_Europe_Music_Awards]  [LINK: ([90]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-90]  and  [LINK: (2007 Kids' Choice Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2007_Kids%27_Choice_Awards] . [LINK: ([91]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-91]  On December 16, 2006, Timberlake hosted  [LINK: (Saturday Night Live) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saturday_Night_Live] , doing double duty as both host and musical guest for the second time. During this appearance, he and  [LINK: (Andy Samberg) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andy_Samberg]  performed an R&B song for a skit titled " [LINK: (Dick in a Box) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dick_in_a_Box] ". [LINK: ([92]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-92]  Called "one of the most iconic musical moments in the show's history" by  [LINK: (Billboard) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_(magazine)] , it became a viral hit and one of the most viewed videos on  [LINK: (YouTube) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/YouTube]  at the time. [LINK: ([93]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-billboard.com-93]   [LINK: (Rolling Stone) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolling_Stone]  listed the skit at number three on their "50 Greatest 'Saturday Night Live' Sketches of All Time". [LINK: ([94]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-94]  The song earned him an  [LINK: (Emmy Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primetime_Emmy_Award_for_Outstanding_Original_Music_and_Lyrics]  [LINK: ([95]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-95]  and was later featured on  [LINK: (The Lonely Island) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Lonely_Island] 's debut album  [LINK: (Incredibad) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incredibad] . [LINK: ([96]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-mtv-96]

In January 2007, Timberlake embarked on the  [LINK: (FutureSex/LoveShow) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FutureSex/LoveShow]  tour. [LINK: ([97]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-97]  Following singles off the album, " [LINK: (LoveStoned/I Think She Knows (Interlude)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LoveStoned] " and " [LINK: (Until the End of Time) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Until_the_End_of_Time_(Justin_Timberlake_and_Beyonc%C3%A9_song)] ", peaked within the top 20 on the Hot 100, [LINK: ([98]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-chart-98]  while the fourth single, " [LINK: (Summer Love) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summer_Love_(Justin_Timberlake_song)] ", reached the top 10. [LINK: ([99]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-99]  The song " [LINK: (Give It to Me) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Give_It_to_Me_(Timbaland_song)] ", a Timbaland single on which Timberlake guests with Nelly Furtado, reached the  [LINK: (Hot 100) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_100]  number-one spot. [LINK: ([100]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-100]  Eventually, FutureSex/LoveSounds was added to the  [LINK: (Rock and Roll Hall of Fame) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_and_Roll_Hall_of_Fame] 's musical library and archive. [LINK: ([101]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-101]

The song " [LINK: (4 Minutes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/4_Minutes] " was first played by  [LINK: (Timbaland) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timbaland]  at Philadelphia's Jingle Ball on December 17, 2007. [LINK: ([102]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-102]  When released on March 17, 2008, "4 Minutes" was revealed to be a duet between Timberlake and  [LINK: (Madonna) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madonna] , with backing vocals by Timbaland. It was the lead single from Madonna's eleventh studio album  [LINK: (Hard Candy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hard_Candy_(Madonna_album)] , which featured four other song-writing collaborations with Timberlake, being also one of the executive producers. [LINK: ([103]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-103]  The single was an international hit, topping the charts in over 21 countries worldwide. [LINK: ([104]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-104]

In June 2007, Timberlake co-wrote, produced and provided vocals for the songs "Nite Runner" and " [LINK: (Falling Down) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Falling_Down_(Duran_Duran_song)] " for  [LINK: (Duran Duran) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duran_Duran] 's album  [LINK: (Red Carpet Massacre) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Carpet_Massacre] , released on November 13, 2007. "Falling Down" was released as a single in the UK on the previous day. [LINK: ([105]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-105]  Also in 2007, Timberlake made an appearance on  [LINK: (50 Cent) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/50_Cent] 's third album  [LINK: (Curtis) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curtis_(50_Cent_album)] . Timberlake, along with Timbaland, is featured on a track called " [LINK: (Ayo Technology) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ayo_Technology] ", which was the album's fourth single. Also, another possible collaboration was to occur with  [LINK: (Lil Wayne) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lil_Wayne]  for his album  [LINK: (Tha Carter III) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tha_Carter_III]  with  [LINK: (Nelly Furtado) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nelly_Furtado]  and Timbaland. [LINK: ([106]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-106]  With the wrapping up of the FutureSex/LoveSounds tour of Australasia and the Middle East in November 2007, Timberlake resumed his film career. Projects underway early in 2008 were starring roles in  [LINK: (Mike Myers) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Myers] ' comedy  [LINK: (The Love Guru) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Love_Guru]  (released June 20, 2008) and Mike Meredith's drama  [LINK: (The Open Road) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Open_Road]  (released August 28, 2009). In March 2008, it was announced that he would be an executive producer in an American adaptation of the hit  [LINK: (Peruvian) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peru]  comedy My Problem with Women for  [LINK: (NBC) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBC] . [LINK: ([107]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-107]  On November 20, 2008,  [LINK: (TV Guide) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TV_Guide]  reported that Timberlake's next single, "Follow My Lead", which also featured vocals by Timberlake's protégée, former YouTube star  [LINK: (Esmée Denters) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Esm%C3%A9e_Denters] , would be available for exclusive download through  [LINK: (Myspace) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myspace] . All proceeds would go to  [LINK: (Shriners Hospitals for Children) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shriners_Hospitals_for_Children] , a charity dedicated to improving pediatric care for sick children. [LINK: ([108]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-108]  In February 2008, Timberlake was awarded two  [LINK: (Grammy Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammy_Award] . At the  [LINK: (50th Grammy Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/50th_Grammy_Awards]  ceremony, he won the  [LINK: (Award for Best Male Pop Vocal Performance) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammy_Award_for_Best_Male_Pop_Vocal_Performance]  for " [LINK: (What Goes Around...Comes Around) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/What_Goes_Around...Comes_Around] ", and the  [LINK: (Award for Best Dance Recording) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammy_Award_for_Best_Dance_Recording]  for " [LINK: (LoveStoned/I Think She Knows) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LoveStoned/I_Think_She_Knows] ". [LINK: ([109]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-109]

In 2008, a collaboration between Timberlake and  [LINK: (T.I.) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T.I.] , " [LINK: (Dead and Gone) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dead_and_Gone] ", was featured on T.I.'s sixth studio album,  [LINK: (Paper Trail) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paper_Trail] , and was released as its fourth single late in 2009. In November 2008, it was confirmed that Timberlake would make a guest appearance and produce some tracks on  [LINK: (R&B) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contemporary_R%26B] / [LINK: (pop) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pop_music]  singer  [LINK: (Ciara) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ciara] 's upcoming album  [LINK: (Fantasy Ride) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fantasy_Ride]  due out May 5, 2009. Timberlake featured on Ciara's second single " [LINK: (Love Sex Magic) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love_Sex_Magic] ", the video being shot on February 20, 2009. [LINK: ([110]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-110]  The single became a worldwide hit, reaching the top ten in numerous countries and peaking at number-one in several countries including Taiwan, India, and Turkey. The song was nominated for  [LINK: (Best Pop Collaboration with Vocals) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Best_Pop_Collaboration_with_Vocals]  at the  [LINK: (52nd Grammy Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/52nd_Grammy_Awards] . Timberlake hosted the 16th  [LINK: (ESPY Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ESPY_Awards] , and the musical number "I Love Sports" was later nominated for an Emmy award. [LINK: ([111]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-111]  Timberlake and his production team  [LINK: (The Y's) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Y%27s] , along with  [LINK: (Mike Elizondo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Elizondo] , produced and co-wrote the song "Don't Let Me Down" for  [LINK: (Leona Lewis) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leona_Lewis] 's second studio album,  [LINK: (Echo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Echo_(Leona_Lewis_album)] , released on November 17, 2009. Timberlake also co-wrote and performed on " [LINK: (Carry Out) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carry_Out] ", the third single from Timbaland's album  [LINK: (Shock Value II) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shock_Value_II] , released on December 1, 2009. [LINK: ([112]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-112]  Timberlake appeared on  [LINK: (Jimmy Fallon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jimmy_Fallon] 's debut as host of  [LINK: (Late Night with Jimmy Fallon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Late_Night_with_Jimmy_Fallon]  on March 2, 2009. [LINK: ([113]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-113]  Timberlake was the executive producer on the  [LINK: (MTV) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MTV]  reality series  [LINK: (The Phone) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Phone_(U.S._TV_series)] , which premiered on April 21, 2009. In late 2009, Barbadian singer  [LINK: (Rihanna) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rihanna]  released the album  [LINK: (Rated R) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rated_R_(Rihanna_album)] , with Timberlake being one of the writers and producers. [LINK: ([114]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-114]  They both worked together previously for her third studio album  [LINK: (Good Girl Gone Bad) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Good_Girl_Gone_Bad] . [LINK: ([115]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-115]

From 2010, Timberlake increased his acting work. He played  [LINK: (Sean Parker) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sean_Parker] , the founder of  [LINK: (Napster) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napster] , in the acclaimed film  [LINK: (The Social Network) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Social_Network]  (2010), [LINK: ([116]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-116]  and voiced  [LINK: (Boo-Boo Bear) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boo-Boo_Bear]  in the live-action/animated comedy film  [LINK: (Yogi Bear) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yogi_Bear_(film)] , adapted from the  [LINK: (Hanna-Barbara series) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Yogi_Bear_Show] . [LINK: ([117]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-117]  He also appeared at the 2010 MTV VMAs on September 12, 2010. [LINK: ([118]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-118]  In 2011, he starred alongside  [LINK: (Cameron Diaz) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cameron_Diaz]  in  [LINK: (Bad Teacher) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bad_Teacher]  and alongside  [LINK: (Mila Kunis) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mila_Kunis]  in  [LINK: (Friends with Benefits) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friends_with_Benefits_(film)] , and played Will Salas, the protagonist of  [LINK: (In Time) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_Time] , a science fiction film by  [LINK: (Andrew Niccol) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_Niccol] . [LINK: ([119]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-119]  He provided a feature and appeared in the music video for the song " [LINK: (Motherlover) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Motherlover] " from  [LINK: (The Lonely Island) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Lonely_Island] 's second album  [LINK: (Turtleneck & Chain) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turtleneck_%26_Chain] , [LINK: ([120]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-120]  and directed and made a cameo in the  [LINK: (FreeSol) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FreeSol]  music video "Hoodies On, Hats Low", which was released in August 2011. [LINK: ([121]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-121]  The Late Night with Jimmy Fallon sketch " [LINK: (History of Rap) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Rap] " was performed for the first time by both Fallon and Timberlake in 2010. [LINK: ([122]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-NYM-122]  In July 2011, United States Marine Kelsey De Santis uploaded a  [LINK: (YouTube) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/YouTube]  video asking Timberlake to be her date to the United States Marine Corps birthday ball; they attended the event on November 13, 2011, in  [LINK: (Richmond, Virginia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richmond,_Virginia] . [LINK: ([123]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-123]  His fifth  [LINK: (Saturday Night Live) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saturday_Night_Live]  episode, as host and musical guest, was the most-watched episode in 14 months, with  [LINK: (Charles Barkley) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Barkley]  as host and  [LINK: (Kelly Clarkson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kelly_Clarkson]  as musical guest. [LINK: ([124]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-124]

Timberlake began working on his third studio album  [LINK: (The 20/20 Experience) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_20/20_Experience]  in June 2012 with "no rules and/or end goal in mind". [LINK: ([125]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-125]  He publicly announced his return to the music industry in January 2013, [LINK: ([126]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-126]  releasing the album's lead single " [LINK: (Suit & Tie) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suit_%26_Tie] " featuring  [LINK: (Jay-Z) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jay-Z]  later that month, which would eventually peak at number three on the Billboard Hot 100. After four years not performing in concert, Timberlake appeared the night before the  [LINK: (2013 Super Bowl) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013_Super_Bowl]  and performed during the " [LINK: (DirecTV) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DirecTV]  Super Saturday Night" on February 2, 2013, in  [LINK: (New Orleans) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Orleans] . [LINK: ([127]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-127]  On February 10, 2013, he performed "Suit & Tie" with sepia-toned lighting at the  [LINK: (55th Annual Grammy Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/55th_Annual_Grammy_Awards] , with Jay-Z joining him from the audience. On February 11, 2013, " [LINK: (Mirrors) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirrors_(Justin_Timberlake_song)] " was released as the second single from The 20/20 Experience. [LINK: ([128]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-128]  The song would eventually peak at number two on the Billboard Hot 100 and number-one on the  [LINK: (UK Singles Chart) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UK_Singles_Chart] . The 20/20 Experience was released on March 19, 2013 [LINK: ([129]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-129]  through  [LINK: (RCA Records) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RCA_Records]  due to the disbandment of  [LINK: (Jive Records) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jive_Records] . [LINK: ([130]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-130]  [LINK: ([131]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-131]  The album set a digital sales record for being the fastest-selling album on the  [LINK: (iTunes Store) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ITunes_Store]  [LINK: ([132]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-132]  and debuted at number-one on the charts by moving just over 968,000 copies in the U.S., the biggest sales week of 2013. [LINK: ([133]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-133]  It eventually became the best-selling album of the year in the country. [LINK: ([134]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-134]

Timberlake performed at the "In Performance at the White House: Memphis Soul" concert, held in the  [LINK: (East Room) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Room]  of the  [LINK: (White House) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_House]  and hosted by President  [LINK: (Barack Obama) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barack_Obama] , celebrating  [LINK: (Memphis soul) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memphis_soul]  music from the 1960s. [LINK: ([135]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-135]  Afterward, Timberlake officially announced  [LINK: (The 20/20 Experience World Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_20/20_Experience_World_Tour] , following his and Jay-Z's co-headlining concert tour  [LINK: (Legends of the Summer Stadium Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Legends_of_the_Summer_Stadium_Tour] . [LINK: ([136]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-136]  Timberlake also appeared on Jay-Z's twelfth studio album  [LINK: (Magna Carta... Holy Grail) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magna_Carta..._Holy_Grail]  on three songs: " [LINK: (Holy Grail) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holy_Grail_(Jay-Z_song)] ", "BBC" (along with  [LINK: (Nas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nas] ,  [LINK: (Swizz Beatz) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swizz_Beatz] , Timbaland,  [LINK: (Pharrell Williams) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pharrell_Williams] , Niigo &  [LINK: (Beyoncé) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beyonc%C3%A9] ), and " [LINK: (Heaven) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heaven_(Jay-Z_song)] ". [LINK: ([137]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-137]  On August 25, 2013, Timberlake received the  [LINK: (Michael Jackson Video Vanguard Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Jackson_Video_Vanguard_Award]  at the  [LINK: (2013 MTV Video Music Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013_MTV_Video_Music_Awards] . He also took home three competitive awards, including  [LINK: (Video of the Year) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MTV_Video_Music_Award_for_Video_of_the_Year]  for "Mirrors". [LINK: ([138]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-vanguard-138]  During his performance, Timberlake briefly reunited with his fellow former NSYNC bandmates for a medley of their hit songs "Girlfriend" and "Bye Bye Bye". [LINK: ([139]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-139]

Timberlake's fourth studio album  [LINK: (The 20/20 Experience – 2 of 2) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_20/20_Experience_%E2%80%93_2_of_2]  was released on September 30, 2013 [LINK: ([140]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-140]  and debuted at number-one on the Billboard 200. [LINK: ([141]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-141]  Its lead single " [LINK: (Take Back the Night) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Take_Back_the_Night_(song)] " was released on July 12, 2013, [LINK: ([142]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-142]  following by the second single " [LINK: (TKO) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TKO_(song)] ". [LINK: ([143]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-143]  Timberlake was given a production and writing credit on  [LINK: (track six) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Partition_(song)]  on  [LINK: (Beyoncé) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beyonc%C3%A9] 's  [LINK: (self-titled fifth studio album) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beyonc%C3%A9_(album)] , which was released in December 2013. [LINK: ([144]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-144]  At the  [LINK: (57th Annual Grammy Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/57th_Annual_Grammy_Awards] , Timberlake was nominated for seven awards, eventually winning three:  [LINK: (Best R&B Song) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Best_R%26B_Song]  for " [LINK: (Pusher Love Girl) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pusher_Love_Girl] ",  [LINK: (Best Rap/Sung Collaboration) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Best_Rap/Sung_Collaboration]  for " [LINK: (Holy Grail) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holy_Grail_(Jay-Z_song)] ", and  [LINK: (Best Music Video) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Best_Music_Video]  for "Suit & Tie", which was directed by The Social Network director  [LINK: (David Fincher) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Fincher] . [LINK: ([145]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-145]  On February 25, 2014, " [LINK: (Not a Bad Thing) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Not_a_Bad_Thing] " was released as the third single from The 20/20 Experience – 2 of 2. [LINK: ([146]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-146]  The song reached the top 10 on the Hot 100 and topped the  [LINK: (Mainstream Top 40) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mainstream_Top_40]  chart. [LINK: ([147]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-147]  In 2014, Timberlake appeared on  [LINK: (Michael Jackson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Jackson] 's second posthumous record  [LINK: (Xscape) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xscape_(album)]  on the song " [LINK: (Love Never Felt So Good) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love_Never_Felt_So_Good] ", which was produced by Timbaland,  [LINK: (Jerome "J-Roc" Harmon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jerome_%22J-Roc%22_Harmon]  and Timberlake. [LINK: ([148]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-148]  On May 14, 2014, a music video was also released featuring clips of Jackson, with Timberlake accompanied by several of Jackson's fans performing some of Jackson's signature moves. The video was directed by Timberlake and  [LINK: (Rich Lee) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rich_Lee] . [LINK: ([149]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-149]  During 2015, Timberlake performed along with  [LINK: (Jimmy Fallon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jimmy_Fallon]  the  [LINK: (Saturday Night Live 40th Anniversary) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saturday_Night_Live_40th_Anniversary_Special] 's cold open, [LINK: ([150]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-150]  returned to  [LINK: (The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Tonight_Show_Starring_Jimmy_Fallon]  as a guest to perform a sixth edition of the sketch " [LINK: (History of Rap) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Rap] ", [LINK: ([151]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-151]  and performed along with  [LINK: (Chris Stapleton) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Stapleton]  at the  [LINK: (49th Annual Country Music Association Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/49th_Annual_Country_Music_Association_Awards] . [LINK: ([152]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-152]

Showcasing the final date of  [LINK: (The 20/20 Experience World Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_20/20_Experience_World_Tour]  at Las Vegas'  [LINK: (MGM Grand Garden Arena) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MGM_Grand_Garden_Arena] , the space-age themed concert film titled  [LINK: (Justin Timberlake + The Tennessee Kids) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake_%2B_The_Tennessee_Kids]  and directed by  [LINK: (Jonathan Demme) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jonathan_Demme]  premiered at the  [LINK: (2016 Toronto International Film Festival) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2016_Toronto_International_Film_Festival]  on September 13. [LINK: ([153]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-153]  [LINK: ([154]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-154]  Timberlake dedicated the film to  [LINK: (Prince) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_(musician)]  for influencing his music. [LINK: ([155]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-155]  Ahead of its debut at the film festival, the streaming service  [LINK: (Netflix) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Netflix]  released it on October 12. [LINK: ([156]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-156]  Timberlake composed the soundtrack and served as music supervisor for the 2017 film  [LINK: (The Book of Love) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Book_of_Love_(film)] , which his wife  [LINK: (Jessica Biel) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jessica_Biel]  produced and starred in. [LINK: ([157]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-157]  [LINK: ([158]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-158]

Timberlake voiced the lead character in  [LINK: (DreamWorks Animation) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DreamWorks_Animation] 's musical comedy  [LINK: (Trolls) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trolls_(film)]  opposite  [LINK: (Anna Kendrick) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anna_Kendrick] . The film was released in November 2016, [LINK: ([159]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-159]  and returned for its next two entries  [LINK: (Trolls: World Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trolls:_World_Tour]  and  [LINK: (Trolls: Band Together) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trolls_Band_Together]  in 2020 and 2023 respectively. [LINK: ([160]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-160]  He also served as the executive music producer, performing  [LINK: (original music for the film) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trolls_(soundtrack)] . [LINK: ([161]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-161]  The lead single, " [LINK: (Can't Stop the Feeling!) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Can%27t_Stop_the_Feeling!] ", was released on May 6, 2016. [LINK: ([162]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-162]  Timberlake was invited by Swedish broadcaster  [LINK: (Sveriges Television) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sveriges_Television]  (SVT) to perform "Can't Stop the Feeling" live during the interval act at the grand finale of the  [LINK: (Eurovision Song Contest 2016) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eurovision_Song_Contest_2016]  on May 14, 2016. [LINK: ([163]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-163]  [LINK: ([164]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-164]  The single debuted at number one on the U.S.  [LINK: (Billboard Hot 100) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Hot_100] , [LINK: ([165]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-hot100numberone-165]  and reached the top spot in other 16 countries. It became his eighth U.S.  [LINK: (Mainstream Top 40) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mainstream_Top_40]  number-one song. [LINK: ([166]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-166]  It became the  [LINK: (best-selling song) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_best-selling_singles_in_the_United_States]  of the year in the U.S. with 2.4 million downloads sold. [LINK: ([167]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-167]  On February 26, 2017, Timberlake opened the  [LINK: (89th Academy Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/89th_Academy_Awards]  with a performance of "Can't Stop the Feeling!", since the song earned him a nomination. [LINK: ([168]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-168]  Also that year, Timberlake starred with  [LINK: (Kate Winslet) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kate_Winslet]  and  [LINK: (Juno Temple) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juno_Temple]  in  [LINK: (Woody Allen) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woody_Allen] 's drama film  [LINK: (Wonder Wheel) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wonder_Wheel_(film)] , [LINK: ([169]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-169]  and headlined several festivals and live sets, including  [LINK: (Rock in Rio) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_in_Rio] , [LINK: ([170]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-170]  the  [LINK: (United States Grand Prix) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Grand_Prix] , [LINK: ([171]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-171]  and the  [LINK: (Pilgrimage Music & Cultural Festival) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pilgrimage_Music_%26_Cultural_Festival] , which he co-produced. [LINK: ([172]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-172]

For the biggest pop stars in the world, the place where they have the most trouble is honesty... Because there's a formulaic sort of vulnerability... But if you're able to really screenshot your own vulnerability, frame it properly, and color-correct it, then it becomes something that every human can relate to. And I think Justin is in the place where he's mastering that right now.

Speaking of his fifth studio album in 2016, Timberlake stated, "I think where I grew up in America has a lot of influence. Growing up in Tennessee—very central of the country—Memphis is known as the birthplace of rock & roll, but also the home of the blues, but Nashville's right down the street so there's a lot of country music." [LINK: ([174]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-174]  In following interviews, Timberlake confirmed working with producers  [LINK: (Timbaland) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timbaland]  and  [LINK: (Pharrell Williams) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pharrell_Williams] , [LINK: ([175]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-175]  while stating, "It sounds more like where I've come from than any other music I've ever made... It's Southern American music. But I want to make it sound modern – at least that's the idea right now." [LINK: ([176]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-176]

His fifth studio album  [LINK: (Man of the Woods) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Man_of_the_Woods]  was released on February 2, 2018, [LINK: ([177]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-177]  two days before he headlined the  [LINK: (Super Bowl LII halftime show) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Bowl_LII_halftime_show]  in  [LINK: (Minneapolis) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minneapolis] ,  [LINK: (Minnesota) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minnesota]  on February 4, where Timberlake performed a medley of his songs featuring both the Tennessee Kids and the  [LINK: (Minnesota Marching Band) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minnesota_Marching_Band]  alongside him, as well as a duet of " [LINK: (I Would Die 4 U) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I_Would_Die_4_U] " with a video projection of late singer  [LINK: (Prince) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_(musician)]  on screen. [LINK: ([178]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-178]  The show contained multiple selections from Man of the Woods, which is named after his son Silas, whose name means "from the forest". [LINK: ([179]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-179]  The album's first single, " [LINK: (Filthy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filthy_(song)] ", was released on January 5, along with its accompanying video directed by  [LINK: (Mark Romanek) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Romanek] . [LINK: ([180]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-180]  The  [LINK: (electro-funk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electro-funk]  song [LINK: ([181]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-181]  has reached number nine in the U.S. [LINK: ([182]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-182]  and number 5 in Canada. [LINK: ([183]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-CanadaHot100-183]  The songs " [LINK: (Supplies) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supplies_(song)] ", " [LINK: (Say Something) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Say_Something_(Justin_Timberlake_song)] " featuring  [LINK: (Chris Stapleton) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Stapleton]  and " [LINK: (Man of the Woods) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Man_of_the_Woods_(song)] " were also released along with music videos ahead of the album. [LINK: ([184]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-184]  His collaboration with Stapleton also reached the top 10 in the U.S. and Canada. [LINK: ([183]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-CanadaHot100-183]  [LINK: ([185]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-185]

Man of the Woods topped the Billboard 200 with the biggest first week sales of the year at the time, selling 293,000 total units. [LINK: ([186]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-186]  Man of the Woods also marks Timberlake's fourth consecutive No. 1 album and has since been certified  [LINK: (Platinum) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_recording_sales_certification]  by the Recording Industry Association of America (RIAA). [LINK: ([187]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-187]  Man of the Woods concluded 2018 as the sixth best-selling album of the year. [LINK: ([188]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-Scorpion-188]  An accompanying  [LINK: (tour of the same name) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Man_of_the_Woods_Tour]  began on March 13, 2018, in  [LINK: (Toronto) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toronto] ,  [LINK: (Canada) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canada]  and concluded on April 13, 2019, in  [LINK: (Uncasville) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uncasville] . [LINK: ([189]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-189]  The Man of the Woods Tour was the sixth-highest-grossing tour of 2018. [LINK: ([190]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-gross-190]

In May 2019, Timberlake received an honorary  [LINK: (doctorate) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doctorate]  from  [LINK: (Berklee College of Music) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berklee_College_of_Music] . [LINK: ([191]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-Honorary-191]   [LINK: (Missy Elliott) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Missy_Elliott]  and  [LINK: (Alex Lacamoire) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alex_Lacamoire]  also received doctorates at the ceremony. [LINK: ([192]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-192]

Following the announcement of  [LINK: (Trolls World Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trolls_World_Tour] , Timberlake teased potential collaborations with a number of artists, through a series of Instagram posts, which included frequent collaborators  [LINK: (Pharrell Williams) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pharrell_Williams] , Nathaniel Hills and  [LINK: (Rob Knox) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rob_Knox_(producer)] , as well as new collaborators such as  [LINK: (Anderson .Paak) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anderson_.Paak] ,  [LINK: (Brandy Norwood) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brandy_Norwood] ,  [LINK: (Lizzo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lizzo] , and  [LINK: (Meek Mill) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meek_Mill] . [LINK: ([193]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-193]  [LINK: ([194]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-194]  [LINK: ([195]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-195]  [LINK: ([196]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-196]  On February 26, 2020,  [LINK: (SZA) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SZA]  and Timberlake released the single " [LINK: (The Other Side) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Other_Side_(SZA_and_Justin_Timberlake_song)] ", a song part of the  [LINK: (Trolls World Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trolls_World_Tour]  soundtrack, alongside its music video. [LINK: ([197]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-197]  [LINK: ([198]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-198]  [LINK: ([199]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-199]  On March 9, 2020, Timberlake released a teaser for his upcoming song "Don't Slack", which features  [LINK: (Anderson .Paak) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anderson_.Paak] , and is also part of the  [LINK: (Trolls World Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trolls_World_Tour]  soundtrack. The song was released on March 10, 2020. [LINK: ([200]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-200]  [LINK: ([201]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-201]

In September 2020, Timberlake and producer Timbaland teased a potential upcoming collaboration with Canadian musician  [LINK: (Justin Bieber) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Bieber] , as well as collaborations with  [LINK: (Justine Skye) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justine_Skye] ,  [LINK: (Hit-Boy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hit-Boy]  and  [LINK: (Ty Dolla Sign) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ty_Dolla_Sign] . [LINK: ([202]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-202]  [LINK: ([203]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-203]  In December 2020, Timberlake and  [LINK: (Ant Clemons) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ant_Clemons]  released the single " [LINK: (Better Days) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Better_Days_(Ant_Clemons_song)] ", which received its premier on the Rock the Runoff virtual concert, held by  [LINK: (Stacey Abrams) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stacey_Abrams] ' organization Fair Fight. [LINK: ([204]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-204]

In January 2021, Timberlake performed as part of the  [LINK: (inauguration of Joe Biden) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inauguration_of_Joe_Biden] . [LINK: ([205]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-205]  [LINK: ([206]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-206]  Performing from his hometown of Memphis, Timberlake performed his collaboration with Ant Clemons during the  [LINK: (Celebrating America) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celebrating_America]  special. [LINK: ([207]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-207]  Timberlake performed at Pharrell Williams' Something in the Water festival in Washington D.C., where he was joined on stage by  [LINK: (T.I.) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T.I.]  and  [LINK: (Clipse) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clipse]  for his five-song set. [LINK: ([208]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-208]

In May 2023, Timbaland revealed that Timberlake's sixth studio album was completed, adding that their pair had revived the sound from the FutureSex/LoveSounds era. [LINK: ([209]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-209]  On September 1, 2023, Timbaland released the single " [LINK: (Keep Going Up) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keep_Going_Up] ", in collaboration with Furtado and Timberlake. Timberlake also reunited with his fellow former band members of  [LINK: (NSYNC) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NSYNC]  later that month and released the single " [LINK: (Better Place) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Better_Place_(NSYNC_song)] " in support of the  [LINK: (Trolls Band Together soundtrack) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trolls_Band_Together_(soundtrack)] . [LINK: ([210]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-et-210]  [LINK: ([211]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-211]  [LINK: ([212]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-212]  [LINK: ([213]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-213]  In addition to "Keep Going Up" and "Better Place", Timberlake had also collaborated with  [LINK: (Meek Mill) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meek_Mill]  on the song  [LINK: (Believe) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Believe_(Meek_Mill_song)] ,  [LINK: (Romeo Santos) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romeo_Santos]  on the song " [LINK: (Sin Fin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sin_Fin] ", [LINK: ([214]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-214]   [LINK: (DJ Khaled) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DJ_Khaled]  on his album  [LINK: (Khaled Khaled) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khaled_Khaled] , on the song "Just Be",  [LINK: (Justine Skye) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justine_Skye]  on her album, Space & Time, on the song "Innocent",  [LINK: (Jack Harlow) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jack_Harlow]  on his album  [LINK: (Come Home the Kids Miss You) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Come_Home_the_Kids_Miss_You] , on the song "Parent Trap"; a remix of  [LINK: (Coco Jones) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coco_Jones] ' " [LINK: (ICU) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ICU_(song)#Remix] " [LINK: ([215]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-remix-215]  and a further remix of the song " [LINK: (3D) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/3D_(song)] " by  [LINK: (Jungkook) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jungkook] . [LINK: ([216]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-Forbes-216]  Timberlake had also worked with  [LINK: (Calvin Harris) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calvin_Harris] , producer of " [LINK: (Fuckin' Up the Disco) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuckin%27_Up_the_Disco] " and " [LINK: (No Angels) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/No_Angels_(Justin_Timberlake_song)] ", on his song " [LINK: (Stay with Me) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stay_with_Me_(Calvin_Harris,_Justin_Timberlake,_Halsey_and_Pharrell_Williams_song)] ", alongside  [LINK: (Pharrell Williams) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pharrell_Williams]  and  [LINK: (Halsey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halsey_(singer)] . [LINK: ([217]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-217]  [LINK: ([218]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-218]

On January 19, 2024, Timberlake performed a free one-night-only concert at the  [LINK: (Orpheum in Memphis) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orpheum_Theatre_(Memphis)]  where he live-debuted his new single " [LINK: (Selfish) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Selfish_(Justin_Timberlake_song)] " after teasing a new project on social media in previous days. [LINK: ([219]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-219]  In promotion of the record, on January 25, 2024, Timberlake appeared on  [LINK: (The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Tonight_Show_Starring_Jimmy_Fallon] ; he announced the release of "Selfish" and revealed that the album had taken four years to produce. [LINK: ([220]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-Zemler-220]

"Selfish" debuted at number 19 on the  [LINK: (Billboard Hot 100) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Hot_100] , marking Timberlake's highest debut in six years on the chart. It became his 39th career solo entry on the Hot 100, and his 29th to reach the top 40. [LINK: ([221]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-221]  On the release day of "Selfish", he also announced that his sixth studio album,  [LINK: (Everything I Thought It Was) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Everything_I_Thought_It_Was] , would be released in March 2024. [LINK: ([222]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-222]  [LINK: ([220]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-Zemler-220]  Timberlake appeared as a musical guest on the January 27, 2024, episode of  [LINK: (Saturday Night Live) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saturday_Night_Live] , singing "Selfish" and "Sanctified". On January 30, he appeared on  [LINK: (The Kelly Clarkson Show) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Kelly_Clarkson_Show]  [LINK: ([223]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-223]  [LINK: ([224]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-224]  and held an "intimate" concert at  [LINK: (Irving Plaza) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irving_Plaza]  in  [LINK: (New York City) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_City]  on January 31, his 43rd birthday. [LINK: ([225]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-225]  He appeared as the musical guest, where he performed "Selfish" on  [LINK: (The Graham Norton Show) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Graham_Norton_Show]  recorded in  [LINK: (London) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/London]  on February 22, 2024, [LINK: ([226]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-226]  the night before he cancelled A One Night Only concert, to be held at the  [LINK: (Roundhouse) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roundhouse_(venue)] , London, on February 23, 2024. Timberlake was recovering from an illness. [LINK: ([227]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-227]  [LINK: ([228]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-228]  The promotional single " [LINK: (Drown) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drown_(Justin_Timberlake_song)] " was released on February 23, 2024. [LINK: ([229]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-229]  [LINK: ([230]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-230]  [LINK: ([231]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-231]  Timberlake also appeared on  [LINK: (Complex Networks) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Complex_Networks]  Sneaker Shopping on March 11, 2024, and mentioned the release of his new album at the end of the video. [LINK: ([232]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-232]

On March 13, 2024, in anticipation of the album release, Timberlake performed a one-off concert at  [LINK: (The Wiltern) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Wiltern]  in Los Angeles. The show featured a surprise reunion with his NSYNC bandmates, with the group playing a medley of hits and the new album track “Paradise.” Timberlake then performed on NPR's Tiny Desk series on March 15 for a half-hour-long concert. [LINK: ([233]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-233]  Timberlake also announced the release of a documentary showing the album's creation process. [LINK: ([234]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-234]  The second single off the record, " [LINK: (No Angels) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/No_Angels_(Justin_Timberlake_song)] ", was released on March 15, 2024, the same day as the album's release. [LINK: ([235]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-235]  Everything I Thought It Was debuted at number four on the U.S.  [LINK: (Billboard 200) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_200] , giving Timberlake his sixth consecutive top five album in the country. [LINK: ([236]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-Ariana_Grande's_'Eternal_Sunshine'-236]

In April 2024, Timberlake opened the  [LINK: (iHeartRadio Music Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_iHeartRadio_Music_Awards] , performing both singles off the album, "Selfish" and "No Angels". [LINK: ([237]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-237]  Timberlake also promoted the album on  [LINK: (the Forget Tomorrow World Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Forget_Tomorrow_World_Tour] , which began on April 29, 2024, in  [LINK: (Vancouver) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vancouver] , Canada. [LINK: ([238]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-238]  On February 23, 2024, Timberlake announced summer 2024 Europe tour dates. [LINK: ([239]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-239]  In March 2024, prior to the tour launching, Trace William Cowen of  [LINK: (Complex) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Complex_(magazine)]  reported that the Forget Tomorrow World Tour had become Timberlake's fastest selling tour to date. They stated that the tour had amassed over $140 million globally in initial ticket sales from over 70 dates and that more than one million attendees are expected. Cowen concluded that "Justin Timberlake's Forget Tomorrow World Tour Is Set to Become His Biggest Yet." [LINK: ([240]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-240]  On May 20, 2024,  [LINK: (Pollstar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pollstar]  announced that nine additional shows were added due to "overwhelming demand" and reported that over 1 million tickets were already sold, becoming Timberlake's fastest selling tour to date. [LINK: ([241]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-241]  The tour received generally positive reviews. [LINK: ([242]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-Vancouver_Sun_1-242]


# PERSONAL LIFE #

In early 1999, Timberlake began dating fellow former  [LINK: (The All New Mickey Mouse Club) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mickey_Mouse_Club#1989–94_revival:_The_All-New_Mickey_Mouse_Club]  cast member and singer  [LINK: (Britney Spears) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Britney_Spears] . Their relationship ended abruptly in March 2002. [LINK: ([243]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-243]  Spears wrote in her 2023 memoir  [LINK: (The Woman in Me) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Woman_in_Me_(memoir)]  that she became pregnant during their relationship and had an abortion in late 2000 after Timberlake said they were not prepared for parenthood and he did not want to be a father. [LINK: ([244]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-244]  [LINK: ([245]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-245]  In 2003, he briefly dated British singer  [LINK: (Emma Bunton) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emma_Bunton] . [LINK: ([246]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-246]  [LINK: ([247]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-247]  [LINK: ([248]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-248]  In April 2003, he began a relationship with actress  [LINK: (Cameron Diaz) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cameron_Diaz]  soon after they met at the  [LINK: (Nickelodeon Kids' Choice Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nickelodeon_Kids%27_Choice_Awards] . After much speculation of breakups throughout their relationship, the couple split in December 2006 shortly after she introduced him as a musical guest on  [LINK: (Saturday Night Live) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saturday_Night_Live] . [LINK: ([249]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-249]  [LINK: ([250]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-250]  [LINK: ([251]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-251]

In January 2007, Timberlake began dating actress  [LINK: (Jessica Biel) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jessica_Biel] . [LINK: ([252]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-252]  They became engaged in December 2011 and married on October 19, 2012, at the Borgo Egnazia resort in  [LINK: (Fasano) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fasano] ,  [LINK: (Italy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italy] . [LINK: ([253]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-253]  Their first child, a son, was born in April 2015. [LINK: ([254]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-254]  [LINK: ([255]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-255]  [LINK: ([256]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-256]  In July 2020, they had a second son. [LINK: ([257]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-257]  [LINK: ([258]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-258]  [LINK: ([259]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-259]

Shortly after midnight on June 18, 2024, Timberlake was arrested in  [LINK: (Sag Harbor, New York) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sag_Harbor,_New_York]  for  [LINK: (driving while intoxicated) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Driving_while_intoxicated]  (DWI). [LINK: ([260]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-arrestandarraignment-260]  [LINK: ([261]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-261]  In addition to being charged with one count of DWI, Timberlake was issued two citations, one for running a stop sign and one for failure to keep in lane. [LINK: ([260]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-arrestandarraignment-260]  He was released nine hours later following his first arraignment at Sag Harbor Village Justice Court. [LINK: ([260]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-arrestandarraignment-260]  The Sag Harbor Police Department would later release his mugshot. [LINK: ([262]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-262]  Timberlake was scheduled to return to court on July 26, 2024. [LINK: ([260]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-arrestandarraignment-260]  [LINK: ([263]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-timberlakearrest-263]  According to his arrest report, Timberlake alleged to authorities that he only had one martini shortly before he was pulled over. [LINK: ([264]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-arrestreport-264]  Despite making this claim, Timberlake refused a  [LINK: (breathalyzer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breathalyzer] . [LINK: ([264]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-arrestreport-264]

On June 22, 2024, bartender employees at the hotel where Timberlake was staying before his DWI arrest confirmed to  [LINK: (People) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People_(magazine)]  that he only had one martini while at the hotel bar. [LINK: ([263]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-timberlakearrest-263]  One employee stating that “If he was drinking more, it wasn't here." [LINK: ([263]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-timberlakearrest-263]  However, according to the arrest report, the officer who pulled Timberlake over after he drove through a stop sign and failed to keep on the right side of the road stated that his "eyes were bloodshot and glassy" at the time, and that "A strong odor of an alcoholic beverage was emanating from his breath, he was unable to divide attention, he had slowed speech, he was unsteady afoot, and he performed poorly on all standardized field sobriety tests." [LINK: ([263]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-timberlakearrest-263]  During the stop, Timberlake reportedly said, "this is going to ruin the tour." The officer, who did not know who Timberlake was, asked "what tour?", to which he replied with "the world tour." [LINK: ([265]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-265]  [LINK: ([266]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-266]  [LINK: ([267]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-267]  That exchange went viral, spawning several memes. [LINK: ([268]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-268]  [LINK: ([269]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-269]  [LINK: ([270]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-270]  Despite the arrest, Timberlake still continued to perform concerts, including a concert in Chicago on June 21, 2024, where he appeared to address the arrest, saying "We've been through ups and downs and lefts and rights... It's been a tough week - but you're here, and I'm here...I know sometimes I'm hard to love, but you keep on loving me and I love you right back." [LINK: ([271]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-271]  [LINK: ([263]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-timberlakearrest-263]

Timberlake, who was performing overseas in Poland, would not attend his July 26, 2024, court arraignment, with his lawyer Edward Burke attending instead. [LINK: ([272]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-july26andmore-272]  Despite Burke's arguments that Timberlake was not intoxicated at the time of his arrest, Sag Harbor Village Justice Carl Irace ordered for Timberlake to be re-arraigned on August 2. [LINK: ([273]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-august2requirement-273]  [LINK: ([274]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-274]  [LINK: ([272]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-july26andmore-272]  For the August 2 arraignment, Timberlake, who was still on tour, appeared virtually from Antwerp, Belgium. [LINK: ([275]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-enterspleaandlicensesuspended-275]  During this arraignment, Timberlake pled not guilty to a revised misdemeanor charge of driving drunk. [LINK: ([275]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-enterspleaandlicensesuspended-275]  Irace also agreed to review Burke's motion to dismiss the DWI charge. [LINK: ([273]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-august2requirement-273]  However, Timberlake's New York license was suspended by the judge for an indeterminate amount of time. [LINK: ([276]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-nbcnewslicense-276]

Timberlake was scheduled to have another hearing on August 9, 2024. [LINK: ([275]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-enterspleaandlicensesuspended-275]  In contrast to the August 2 hearing, Timberlake was not required to attend this court hearing. [LINK: ([277]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-277]  On September 11, 2024, it was revealed that Timberlake would plead guilty to a less serious traffic offense during his September 13 court appearance, with the DWI charge being dropped. [LINK: ([278]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-278]  [LINK: ([279]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-279]  [LINK: ([280]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-280]  Under his plea deal, Timberlake agreed to plead guilty to driving while impaired, a lesser offense which carries a penalty of a $300 to $500 fine and a 90-day driver license suspension. [LINK: ([281]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-281]

On September 13, 2024, during an in-person appearance at the Sag Harbor Village Justice Courthouse, Timberlake pled guilty to a noncriminal driving while impaired traffic violation. [LINK: ([282]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-282]  Irace then sentenced Timberlake to a $500 fine with a $260 surcharge, 25 hours of community service at the nonprofit of his choosing and required him to make a public safety announcement. [LINK: ([283]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-pleaandsentencemade-283]  It also revealed that Timberlake's refusal to take a breathlyzer automatically triggered a suspension of his driver's license under New York state law. [LINK: ([283]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-pleaandsentencemade-283]

In July 2002, Timberlake purchased a 13,250-square-foot (1,231 m2) mansion in  [LINK: (Hollywood Hills) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hollywood_Hills]  for $8.3 million from  [LINK: (Helen Hunt) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helen_Hunt] . [LINK: ([284]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-284]  In 2010, Timberlake purchased a unit at 311 West Broadway in  [LINK: (SoHo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SoHo] , formerly owned by  [LINK: (Oscar de la Renta) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oscar_de_la_Renta] , for $6.56 million. He sold the unit in 2018 for $6.35 million, incurring a loss. [LINK: ([285]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-285]  [LINK: ([286]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-286]

In 2015, Timberlake bought a house in the  [LINK: (Yellowstone Club) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellowstone_Club]  near  [LINK: (Big Sky, Montana) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Sky,_Montana] . [LINK: ([287]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-287]  [LINK: ([288]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-288]  In May 2017, Timberlake and his wife,  [LINK: (Jessica Biel) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jessica_Biel] , paid $20.2 million for a 5,375-square-foot (499.4 m2)  [LINK: (penthouse) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penthouse_apartment]  unit at 443 Greenwich Street in  [LINK: (Tribeca) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tribeca] ,  [LINK: (Manhattan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan] . [LINK: ([289]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-289]

[LINK: (Forbes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forbes]  began reporting on Timberlake's earnings in 2008, calculating that he earned $44 million between June 2007 and June 2008 for his music, tour, commercials, and hospitality, making him the world's 4th best-paid music personality at the time, above  [LINK: (Madonna) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madonna]  and  [LINK: (Celine Dion) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celine_Dion] . [LINK: ([290]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-290]  That year, he was ranked twelfth on the  [LINK: (Forbes Celebrity 100) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forbes_Celebrity_100]  list [LINK: ([291]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-291]  and second on the "Best-Paid Celebrities Under 30" list. [LINK: ([292]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-292]

According to Billboard, Timberlake was the third highest-paid musician of 2013, with earnings of $31 million. [LINK: ([293]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-293]  He was ranked 26th with earnings of $57 million on the Celebrity 100 list for 2014, [LINK: ([294]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-294]  and 19th on the 2015 list with $63 million. [LINK: ([295]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-295]  Timberlake was listed at number three on the Billboard Money-Makers List of 2014. [LINK: ([296]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-296]

He was ranked 41st on the 2019 Celebrity 100 list by  [LINK: (Forbes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forbes] , with earnings of $57.5 million in 2019. [LINK: ([297]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-297]

At the end of his  [LINK: (Forget Tomorrow World Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forget_Tomorrow_World_Tour]  in July 2025, Timberlake stated he had been diagnosed with  [LINK: (Lyme disease) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lyme_disease] . He shared, in an Instagram post, "When I first got the diagnosis I was shocked for sure. But, at least I could understand why I would be onstage and in a massive amount of nerve pain or, just feeling crazy fatigue or sickness. I was faced with a personal decision. Stop touring? Or, keep going and figure it out. I decided the joy that performing brings me far outweighs the fleeting stress my body was feeling. I'm so glad I kept going". [LINK: ([298]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-298]  [LINK: ([299]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-299]


# ARTISTRY #

Timberlake possesses a lyric  [LINK: (tenor) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tenor]   [LINK: (vocal range) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voice_type] . [LINK: ([300]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-300]  He began including  [LINK: (beatboxing) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beatboxing]  in his records near the end of his boyband era and into his emergence as a solo act with Justified and FutureSex/LoveSounds. [LINK: ([301]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-301]  [LINK: ([302]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-302]  [LINK: ([303]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-303]  Many of his songs draw from his personal life and relationships, such as " [LINK: (Cry Me a River) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cry_Me_a_River_(Justin_Timberlake_song)] " (about his breakup with  [LINK: (Britney Spears) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Britney_Spears] ). [LINK: ([304]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-304]  [LINK: ([305]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-305]  Described by critics as a "consummate showman", [LINK: ([306]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-hbjt-306]  [LINK: ([307]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-307]  Timberlake usually plays guitar, piano and keyboard in his shows. [LINK: ([308]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-308]  The New York Times' editor Katie Rogers highlighted Timberlake's crossover appeal after his performance with  [LINK: (Chris Stapleton) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Stapleton]  at the  [LINK: (2015 Country Music Association Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/49th_Annual_Country_Music_Association_Awards] . [LINK: ([309]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-309]

Primarily an R&B album, his 2002 debut  [LINK: (Justified) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justified_(album)]  also includes influence from  [LINK: (dance-pop) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance-pop] ,  [LINK: (funk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Funk]  and  [LINK: (soul) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soul_music]  music. [LINK: ([310]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-310]  Timberlake has described it as influenced by  [LINK: (Michael Jackson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Jackson]  and  [LINK: (Stevie Wonder) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stevie_Wonder] . [LINK: ([78]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-backsexy-78]  For the album's supporting tour  [LINK: (Justified and Stripped Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justified_and_Stripped_Tour] , he co-headlined with  [LINK: (Christina Aguilera) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christina_Aguilera] , drawing praise from  [LINK: (Robert Hilburn) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Hilburn]  of the  [LINK: (Los Angeles Times) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Angeles_Times]  for his comfort in performing as part of a package. [LINK: ([311]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-311]

His 2006 followup album  [LINK: (FutureSex/LoveSounds) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FutureSex/LoveSounds]  departed from his earlier work to explore a broader sound, with elements of  [LINK: (rap) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rap_(music)] ,  [LINK: (rock) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_music] ,  [LINK: (funk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Funk] ,  [LINK: (soul) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soul_music] ,  [LINK: (gospel) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gospel_music] ,  [LINK: (new wave) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_wave_music] ,  [LINK: (opera) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opera] , and  [LINK: (world music) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_music] . [LINK: ([312]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-FOOTNOTEVineyard2006-312]  [LINK: ([78]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-backsexy-78]  [LINK: ([313]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-313]  [LINK: ([314]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-FOOTNOTECollis20071-314]  During production, Timberlake was interested in musical techniques associated with rock music, which inspired his approach to recording. [LINK: ([55]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-revs_up-55]  [LINK: ([315]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-315]  He described the album as drawing from  [LINK: (David Bowie) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Bowie]  and  [LINK: (Prince) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_(musician)] . [LINK: ([78]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-backsexy-78]  Other influences include late  [LINK: (INXS) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/INXS] -frontman  [LINK: (Michael Hutchence) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Hutchence] , [LINK: ([316]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-Moss_p_1-316]   [LINK: (Arcade Fire) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arcade_Fire] ,  [LINK: (David Byrne) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Byrne] ,  [LINK: (The Killers) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Killers] ,  [LINK: (The Strokes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Strokes] , and  [LINK: (Radiohead) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radiohead] . [LINK: ([317]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-FOOTNOTEScaggs20064-317]

Timberlake's next album,  [LINK: (The 20/20 Experience) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_20/20_Experience]  (2013) is a neo soul album partly inspired by the expansive song structures of 1960s and 1970s rock. [LINK: ([318]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-318]  Mikael Wood of the  [LINK: (Los Angeles Times) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Angeles_Times]  found its elaborate structures ambitious in the vein of Stevie Wonder, Prince, and Michael Jackson. [LINK: ([319]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-Wood-319]  He supported the album with a pair of tours:  [LINK: (Legends of the Summer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Legends_of_the_Summer_Stadium_Tour] , which he co-headlined with  [LINK: (Jay-Z) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jay-Z] , and  [LINK: (The 20/20 Experience World Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_20/20_Experience_World_Tour] . [LINK: ([320]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-announcement-320]  [LINK: ([321]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-321]  These tours introduced his backing ensemble, the Tennessee Kids, a 15-piece multi-instrumentalist throwback to  [LINK: (big band) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_band]  music. [LINK: ([322]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-322]  [LINK: ([323]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-323]


# PUBLIC IMAGE #

Timberlake's fashion and style evolution, from "boy-band synchronized wardrobe days" to "a notable source of fashion inspiration to men all over", has been noticed by the media. [LINK: ([324]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-324]  [LINK: ([325]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-325]  As noted by a Billboard editor, "Since his solo career began with the 2002 release of debut album Justified, Timberlake has honed his unique sense of style", while citing  [LINK: (Elvis Presley) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elvis_Presley] ,  [LINK: (Johnny Cash) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johnny_Cash] ,  [LINK: (Jerry Lee Lewis) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jerry_Lee_Lewis]  and  [LINK: (Frank Sinatra) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frank_Sinatra]  as style influences: "guys who were just really never trying to be that [stylish], they just were that". [LINK: ([326]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-326]  According to American fashion designer  [LINK: (Tom Ford) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom_Ford] , who has dressed Timberlake since 2011 and created more than 600 exclusive pieces for  [LINK: (The 20/20 Experience World Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_20/20_Experience_World_Tour] , Timberlake "has a kind of effortless cool that makes classic menswear tailoring modern". [LINK: ([327]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-327]

[LINK: (The New York Times) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times] ' editor Sia Michel wrote in 2007, "Since his last tour, for 2002's multiplatinum Justified, he has learned how to project sex-symbol edge" adding "he's a rock star who can commit." [LINK: ([328]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-Bringing-328]  [LINK: ([329]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-329]   [LINK: (Napster) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napster] 's founder  [LINK: (Sean Parker) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sean_Parker] , portrayed by Timberlake in  [LINK: (The Social Network) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Social_Network] , stated "I don't think I look anything like Timberlake, but it's not so bad being played by a sex symbol." [LINK: ([330]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-330]  In  [LINK: (Nielsen Music) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nielsen_N.V.] 's U.S. report for 2015, Timberlake led the "Top 10 Musicians Among  [LINK: (Millennials) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millennials] " list. [LINK: ([331]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-331]  His high-profile relationships earned him the nickname "Trousersnake", a reference to his allegedly big  [LINK: (penis) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penis] . [LINK: ([332]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-332]  [LINK: ([333]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-333]  [LINK: ([334]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-334]  Wax statues of Timberlake are on display at the  [LINK: (Madame Tussauds) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madame_Tussauds]  wax museums in New York, [LINK: ([335]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-335]  Las Vegas, [LINK: ([336]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-336]  Hollywood, [LINK: ([337]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-337]  Nashville, [LINK: ([338]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-338]  Berlin, [LINK: ([339]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-339]  Amsterdam, [LINK: ([340]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-340]  and London. [LINK: ([341]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-341]  His costume used in the  [LINK: (Saturday Night Live) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saturday_Night_Live]  skit " [LINK: (Dick in a Box) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dick_in_a_Box] " is displayed at "Saturday Night Live: The Exhibition" in New York. [LINK: ([342]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-342]

After New York legalized  [LINK: (same-sex marriage) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Same-sex_marriage_in_New_York]  in 2011, he voiced his support for  [LINK: (LGBT equality) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LGBT_equality]  in the U.S., stating, "We're people and we're different, all of us. And we should be using our differences to bring ourselves closer together." [LINK: ([343]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-glsen-343]  [LINK: ([344]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-344]  Timberlake and his wife  [LINK: (Jessica Biel) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jessica_Biel]  received the Inspiration Award at the  [LINK: (GLSEN Respect Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GLSEN_Respect_Awards]  in 2015, with the executive director saying, "They are two vocal and committed  [LINK: (allies) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Straight_ally]  to the LGBT community who are also devoted to charitable works that improve the lives of youth." [LINK: ([343]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-glsen-343]

Timberlake's pronunciation of the word "me" on " [LINK: (It's Gonna Be Me) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/It%27s_Gonna_Be_Me] " was popularized as an  [LINK: (internet meme) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_meme]  titled "It's Gonna Be May", after a  [LINK: (Tumblr) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tumblr]  image of Timberlake was posted in 2012 with the respective caption. [LINK: ([345]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-345]  The meme eventually became an annually recurring joke throughout the month of April, [LINK: ([346]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-Vox-346]  [LINK: ([347]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-347]  which gained the attention of  [LINK: (Barack Obama) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barack_Obama]  and Timberlake himself. [LINK: ([348]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-348]  Influenced by the national attention received by Timberlake's selfie inside a  [LINK: (voting booth) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voting_booth]  shared on  [LINK: (Instagram) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instagram]  during the 2016 presidential election, which was at the moment an illegal act, [LINK: ([349]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-349]  Senator  [LINK: (Brian Kelsey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brian_Kelsey]  of  [LINK: (Germantown, Tennessee) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germantown,_Tennessee]  brought up a bill that would allow taking photos in voting poll stations, with some exceptions against bad procedures. It was later approved by the  [LINK: (Tennessee Senate) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tennessee_Senate] . [LINK: ([350]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-350]

In June 2021, Timberlake spoke out in support of Britney Spears during her  [LINK: (court battle over her conservatorship) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Britney_Spears_conservatorship_dispute] . Timberlake wrote on his Twitter that "No woman should ever be restricted from making decisions about her own body [...] [Jessica Biel] and I send our love, and our absolute support to Britney during this time. We hope the courts, and her family make this right and let her live however she wants to live". [LINK: ([351]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-351]

Following the release of  [LINK: (Framing Britney Spears) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Framing_Britney_Spears] , public attention was brought to old comments Timberlake made in 2002 to describe his relationship with  [LINK: (Britney Spears) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Britney_Spears]  following their breakup, with some considering them to contain misogynistic rhetoric. [LINK: ([352]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-352]  It also led to renewed interest in his participation in the  [LINK: (Super Bowl XXXVIII halftime show controversy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Bowl_XXXVIII_halftime_show_controversy] , where he exposed  [LINK: (Janet Jackson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janet_Jackson] 's breast on live television. Following much public pressure, Timberlake issued a public apology on his Instagram page, writing he "benefited from a system that condones misogyny and racism" and "I do not want to ever benefit from others being pulled down again." He finished by saying "I care deeply about the wellbeing of the people I love and have loved. I can do better and I will do better". [LINK: ([353]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-353]

Public scrutiny surrounding the Super Bowl XXXVIII incident was raised when a stylist alleged that the plan was originally for Timberlake to step on the back of Jackson's dress "to reveal her butt in this pearl g-string" but that he changed the plan to exposing her breast because he wanted a "reveal" to  "one-up" Britney Spears' and  [LINK: (Madonna) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madonna] 's kiss at the  [LINK: (2003 MTV Video Music Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2003_MTV_Video_Music_Awards] . [LINK: ([354]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-354]  [LINK: ([355]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-355]  [LINK: ([356]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-356]  The claim that Timberlake wanted the breast reveal, however, is contradictory to a statement from Salli Frattini, the producer of the Halftime show, who stated in 2018 that the production team experimented with removing elements of clothing in rehearsal to reveal Jackson's skirt without nudity but that the idea was ultimately nixed. According to Frattini, it was Jackson's team who pitched the idea to Timberlake prior to the show that led to Jackson's breast being exposed. [LINK: ([357]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-357]


# LEGACY #

Timberlake has been referred to as the " [LINK: (President of Pop) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honorific_nicknames_in_popular_music] " [LINK: ([358]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-358]  and "Prince of Pop" [LINK: ([359]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-359]  by contemporary journalists. [LINK: ([360]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-360]  In a 2016 article of  [LINK: (The Hollywood Reporter) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Hollywood_Reporter] , editor Scott Feinberg stated Timberlake is "widely regarded as one of the greatest all-around entertainers in the history of show business". [LINK: ([361]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-361]

In 2003,  [LINK: (Rolling Stone) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolling_Stone]  named him the biggest pop star of the year and featured him on the magazine's cover, declaring he was "The New King of Pop". [LINK: ([11]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-rsinterview-11]  For  [LINK: (Entertainment Weekly) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Entertainment_Weekly]  his second studio album, FutureSex/LoveSounds, "redefined pop's cutting edge"; [LINK: ([362]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-ewdecade-362]  for  [LINK: (Vibe) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vibe_(magazine)]  it "pushed boundaries more forcefully" than works by his male contemporaries. [LINK: ([363]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-vibe-363]   [LINK: (Fuse TV) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuse_TV] 's editor Jason Lipshutz stated it "changed the game. [The album] was steely and sweaty, a universal dance opus that made room for intimacy. It had the best first half of any pop album in 25 years. You have to go back to 1979 for  [LINK: (Off the Wall) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Off_the_Wall] , to find a pop album with a first half that matches up." [LINK: ([364]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-364]  He was ranked 66th on the  [LINK: (VH1) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/VH1]  100 Greatest Artists of All-Time. [LINK: ([365]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-365]  Timberlake appeared for the first time on the  [LINK: (Time 100) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_100]  list of most influential people by  [LINK: (Time) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_(magazine)]  in 2007. [LINK: ([366]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-366]  In 2013, he made his second appearance on the 100 list, with  [LINK: (Stevie Wonder) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stevie_Wonder]  writing "Justin has accomplished a lot at a young age, taking advantage of all the possibilities, and yet he's found time to give of himself too—he gets and gives back. He has a spirit. He does God's work through using the most of his talent." [LINK: ([367]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-time2013-367]

Justified's single " [LINK: (Cry Me a River) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cry_Me_a_River_(Justin_Timberlake_song)] " was ranked at number 20 on  [LINK: (Rolling Stone) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolling_Stone] 's 100 Best Songs of the 2000s, and one of their  [LINK: (500 greatest songs of all time) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolling_Stone%27s_500_Greatest_Songs_of_All_Time] . [LINK: ([368]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-368]  [LINK: ([369]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-369]   [LINK: (Billboard) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_(magazine)]  editor Jason Lipshutz named the song's music video "one of the more brilliant musical moments in pop music since the dawn of the century". [LINK: ([370]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-370]  His second album  [LINK: (FutureSex/LoveSounds) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FutureSex/LoveSounds]  was placed at 46 on Rolling Stone's 100 Best Albums of the 2000s, [LINK: ([371]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-371]  the ninth best album of the decade for  [LINK: (Entertainment Weekly) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Entertainment_Weekly] , [LINK: ([362]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-ewdecade-362]  and the greatest of the decade for  [LINK: (Vibe) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vibe_(magazine)] . [LINK: ([363]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-vibe-363]  The lead single, " [LINK: (SexyBack) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SexyBack] ", helped introduce  [LINK: (EDM) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electronic_Dance_Music]  sounds to  [LINK: (top 40 radio) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Top_40_radio] , as it brought together variations of electronic dance music with Timberlake's R&B tone. [LINK: ([372]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-372]  [LINK: ([373]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-373]  Aside from earning critical acclaim for its parent album, Sia Michel of  [LINK: (The New York Times) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times]  noted that he was responsible for popularizing in 2006 the catchphrase "I'm bringing sexy back". [LINK: ([314]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-FOOTNOTECollis20071-314]  [LINK: ([328]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-Bringing-328]  [LINK: ([374]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-374]

Considered a  [LINK: (pop icon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pop_icon]  by media outlets, [LINK: ([375]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-375]  his work has influenced numerous artists, including  [LINK: (Justin Bieber) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Bieber] , [LINK: ([376]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-376]   [LINK: (Shawn Mendes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shawn_Mendes] , [LINK: ([377]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-377]   [LINK: (Olly Murs) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olly_Murs] , [LINK: ([378]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-378]   [LINK: (Maroon 5) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maroon_5] , [LINK: ([379]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-379]   [LINK: (Britney Spears) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Britney_Spears] , [LINK: ([380]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-380]   [LINK: (Lorde) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lorde] , [LINK: ([381]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-381]   [LINK: (Marilyn Manson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marilyn_Manson] , [LINK: ([382]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-382]   [LINK: (Joe Jonas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joe_Jonas] , [LINK: ([383]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-383]   [LINK: (Thomas Rhett) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Rhett] , [LINK: ([384]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-384]   [LINK: (Ed Sheeran) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ed_Sheeran] , [LINK: ([385]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-385]   [LINK: (Jason Derulo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jason_Derulo] , [LINK: ([386]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-386]   [LINK: (Tori Kelly) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tori_Kelly] , [LINK: ([387]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-387]   [LINK: (Liam Payne) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liam_Payne] , [LINK: ([388]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-388]  [LINK: ([389]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-389]   [LINK: (Bridgit Mendler) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bridgit_Mendler] , [LINK: ([390]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-390]   [LINK: (Hunter Hayes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunter_Hayes] , [LINK: ([391]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-391]   [LINK: (BoA) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BoA] , [LINK: ([392]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-392]   [LINK: (Seungri) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seungri] , [LINK: ([393]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-393]  [LINK: ([394]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-394]   [LINK: (Taeyang) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taeyang] , [LINK: ([395]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-395]   [LINK: (Rain) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rain_(entertainer)] , [LINK: ([396]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-396]  [LINK: ([397]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-397]   [LINK: (Lloyd Banks) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lloyd_Banks] , [LINK: ([398]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-398]   [LINK: (Maluma) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maluma] , [LINK: ([399]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-399]   [LINK: (Rosalía) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosal%C3%ADa] , [LINK: ([400]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-400]  and  [LINK: (Jungkook) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jungkook] . [LINK: ([401]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-401]  Bieber and  [LINK: (Nick Jonas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nick_Jonas]  have cited him as one of their role models, with the latter stating is for "not only transitioning from where he started, but also balancing acting and singing". [LINK: ([402]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-402]  [LINK: ([403]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-403]  Christian hip hop artist  [LINK: (tobyMac) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TobyMac]  has stated Timberlake's work inspires him, commenting "he's setting himself up to be a classic, making decisions and moving on them. That's a great place to be." [LINK: ([404]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-404]  In the context of male artists that achieved commercial success after leaving their boy bands, Brittany Spanos from  [LINK: (Rolling Stone) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolling_Stone]  wrote "Timberlake and  [LINK: (Michael Jackson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Jackson]  set a high bar for what could be attained by solo success in that they not only scored numerous number-one hits but they also crafted the mold for what it meant to be a male pop star", [LINK: ([405]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-405]  while for  [LINK: (Variety) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Variety_(magazine)] 's Jeremy Blacklow the singer is "the modern case study". [LINK: ([406]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-406]  Multiple music publications have deemed Justified as the standard for post boy-band solo albums and teen pop stars seeking credibility. [LINK: ([407]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-407]  [LINK: ([408]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-408]  [LINK: ([409]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-409]   [LINK: (Billboard) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_(magazine)]  critics discussed in 2018 whether Timberlake is "the Best Male Pop Star of the 21st century;" those in favor named his crossover appeal, career longevity, showmanship and credibility within the industry among the reasons. [LINK: ([410]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-410]


# ACHIEVEMENTS #

Throughout his solo career, Timberlake has sold over 32 million albums and 56 million singles globally, and a further 70 million records with NSYNC, making him one of the  [LINK: (world's best-selling music artists) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World%27s_best-selling_music_artists] . [LINK: ([33]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-nsync_records-33]  [LINK: ([411]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-411]  Timberlake has won ten  [LINK: (Grammy Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammy_Award] , four  [LINK: (Emmy Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emmy_Award] , seven  [LINK: (American Music Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Music_Award] , three  [LINK: (Brit Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brit_Awards] , nine  [LINK: (Billboard Music Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Music_Awards] , and eleven  [LINK: (MTV Video Music Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MTV_Video_Music_Award] . His Grammy wins include  [LINK: (categories) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Grammy_Award_categories]  on the pop, dance and R&B genres; [LINK: ([412]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-412]  while his Emmy wins consist of two  [LINK: (Outstanding Original Music and Lyrics) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primetime_Emmy_Award_for_Outstanding_Original_Music_and_Lyrics]  and two  [LINK: (Outstanding Guest Actor in a Comedy Series) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primetime_Emmy_Award_for_Outstanding_Guest_Actor_in_a_Comedy_Series] . [LINK: ([413]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-413]  Timberlake received the  [LINK: (Michael Jackson Video Vanguard Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Jackson_Video_Vanguard_Award]  at the  [LINK: (2013 MTV Video Music Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013_MTV_Video_Music_Awards]  [LINK: ([138]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-vanguard-138]  and the  [LINK: (Innovator Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IHeartRadio_Music_Awards#iHeartRadio_Innovator_Award]  at the  [LINK: (2015 iHeartRadio Music Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2015_iHeartRadio_Music_Awards] . [LINK: ([414]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-newsiheart-414]  Among other awards, he won the  [LINK: (MTV Video Music Award for Video of the Year) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MTV_Video_Music_Award_for_Video_of_the_Year]  for "Mirrors" in 2013 and the  [LINK: (Billboard Music Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Music_Award]  for  [LINK: (Top Artist) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Music_Award_for_Top_Artist]  with the  [LINK: (Top Billboard 200 Album) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Music_Award_for_Top_Billboard_200_Album]  for The 20/20 Experience in 2014. Timberlake received the inaugural Decade Award at the  [LINK: (2016 Teen Choice Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2016_Teen_Choice_Awards]  for his continuous achievements since the release of  [LINK: (FutureSex/LoveSounds) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FutureSex/LoveSounds]  (2006). [LINK: ([415]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-415]

In October 2015, he was inducted into the  [LINK: (Memphis Music Hall of Fame) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memphis_Music_Hall_of_Fame] , becoming its youngest member. [LINK: ([416]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-416]  [LINK: ([417]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-417]  On April 30, 2018, Timberlake reunited with his NSYNC bandmates to receive a star on the  [LINK: (Hollywood Walk of Fame) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hollywood_Walk_of_Fame] . [LINK: ([418]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-418]  In 2019, Timberlake received a Contemporary Icon Award by the  [LINK: (Songwriters Hall of Fame) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Songwriters_Hall_of_Fame] , [LINK: ([419]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-419]  and an honorary  [LINK: (Doctor of Music) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doctor_of_Music]  degree from  [LINK: (Berklee College of Music) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berklee_College_of_Music] . [LINK: ([420]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-420]

All five of Timberlake's studio albums have been certified  [LINK: (platinum) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_recording_sales_certification]  or better by the  [LINK: (RIAA) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RIAA]  and have received numerous awards. Worldwide sales figures for  [LINK: (Justified) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justified_(album)]  stand at 10 million copies, [LINK: ([421]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-421]   [LINK: (FutureSex/LoveSounds) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FutureSex/LoveSounds]  at 10 million, [LINK: ([422]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-422]  and joint sales of  [LINK: (The 20/20 Experience) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_20/20_Experience]  and  [LINK: (2 of 2) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_20/20_Experience_%E2%80%93_2_of_2]  at 6 million copies. [LINK: ([423]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-423]  As of 2014 [LINK: ([update]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Justin_Timberlake&action=edit] , Timberlake has had seven songs exceed 3 million digital downloads in the United States, with " [LINK: (SexyBack) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SexyBack] " (4.5), [LINK: ([424]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-424]  " [LINK: (4 Minutes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/4_Minutes] ", [LINK: ([425]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-threem-425]  " [LINK: (Dead and Gone) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dead_and_Gone] ", [LINK: ([425]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-threem-425]  " [LINK: (Suit & Tie) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suit_%26_Tie] ", [LINK: ([426]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-Grein-426]  " [LINK: (Mirrors) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirrors_(Justin_Timberlake_song)] ", [LINK: ([427]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-427]  " [LINK: (Holy Grail) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holy_Grail_(Jay_Z_song)] ", [LINK: ([426]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-Grein-426]  and " [LINK: (Can't Stop the Feeling!) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Can%27t_Stop_the_Feeling!] ". [LINK: ([428]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-428]

According to Billboard,  [LINK: (FutureSex/LoveShow) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FutureSex/LoveShow]  was the third highest-grossing concert tour of 2007 and highest solo. [LINK: ([429]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-429]   [LINK: (The 20/20 Experience World Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_20/20_Experience_World_Tour]  was an international success and became Timberlake's most successful tour to date. The tour was the highest-grossing led by a solo artist in 2014, and one of the  [LINK: (highest-grossing tours of the decade) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Highest_grossing_tours] . [LINK: ([430]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-430]  For its associated album,  [LINK: (The 20/20 Experience) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_20/20_Experience] , Timberlake was named 2013 Artist of the Year with the top-selling album by  [LINK: (iTunes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ITunes] ' annual list of best-sellers. [LINK: ([431]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-431]

In the United States, five of Timberlake's singles have topped the  [LINK: (Billboard Hot 100) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Hot_100] : " [LINK: (SexyBack) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SexyBack] ", " [LINK: (My Love) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/My_Love_(Justin_Timberlake_song)] " and " [LINK: (What Goes Around... Comes Around) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/What_Goes_Around..._Comes_Around] ", " [LINK: (Give It to Me) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Give_It_to_Me_(Timbaland_song)] " and "Can't Stop the Feeling!". [LINK: ([165]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-hot100numberone-165]  The latter became the 41st Hot 100 number one song to be nominated for an  [LINK: (Academy Award for Best Original Song) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Academy_Award_for_Best_Original_Song] . [LINK: ([432]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-432]  He topped nine  [LINK: (Billboard Year-End charts) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Year-End]  for 2013, including Billboard 200 Artists [LINK: ([433]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-433]  and Billboard 200 Albums. [LINK: ([434]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-434]  For 2014, Timberlake was named Billboard Top Male Artist. [LINK: ([435]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-435]  Billboard published a list of "Greatest of All Time  [LINK: (Pop Songs) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pop_Songs]  Artists" in 2017, where Timberlake ranked at number 5, being the top male soloist. [LINK: ([436]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-436]  The magazine also ranked him 25 on their "The Top 60 Male Artists of All-Time" list in 2018, [LINK: ([437]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-437]  and 64th on "The Hot 100's Top Artists of All Time". [LINK: ([438]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-438]  In 2019, Billboard ranked him 20th on their decade-end chart for "Top Artists" of the 2010s, [LINK: ([439]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-439]  and 74th on "Top 125 Greatest of All Time Artists Chart". [LINK: ([440]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-440]


# OTHER VENTURES #

Timberlake has co-owned or provided celebrity endorsement for three restaurants in the United States: "Chi" opened in  [LINK: (West Hollywood, California) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Hollywood,_California]  in 2003, [LINK: ([441]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-441]  and "Destino" and "Southern Hospitality" in New York opened in 2006 and 2007, respectively. [LINK: ([442]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-442]  In 2005, Timberlake launched the  [LINK: (William Rast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Rast]  clothing line with childhood friend Juan ("Trace") Ayala. The 2007 line contained cord jackets, cashmere sweaters, jeans, and polo shirts. [LINK: ([443]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-443]  The pair reports inspiration from fellow Memphis resident  [LINK: (Elvis Presley) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elvis_Presley] : "Elvis is the perfect mixture of Justin and I", Ayala says. "You can go back and see pictures of him in cowboy boots and a cowboy hat and a nice button-down shirt, but then again you can see him in a tux and a collared shirt with rhinestones on it and slacks. We like to think 'If he was alive today, what would he be wearing?'" [LINK: ([444]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-444]  Target has announced that a William Rast collection, including denim, outerwear and sportswear for men and women, would launch in December and be available for a month. [LINK: ([445]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-445]  In 2015, the clothing line earned him a  [LINK: (Lord & Taylor) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lord_%26_Taylor] 's Fashion Oracle Award at the  [LINK: (Fashion Group International) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fashion_Group_International] 's Night of The Stars Gala. [LINK: ([446]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-446]  An avid amateur golfer, in 2007 Timberlake purchased the run-down Big Creek Golf Course in his hometown of  [LINK: (Millington, Tennessee) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millington,_Tennessee] , which he redeveloped as the  [LINK: (eco-friendly) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eco-friendly]  Mirimichi Golf Course at the cost of around $US16 million. It was reopened on July 25, 2009, but closed again on January 15, 2010, for further improvements expected to take six months. [LINK: ([447]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-447]  In October 2011, Timberlake received the Futures Award at the  [LINK: (Environmental Media Awards) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Environmental_Media_Awards]  for his green-conscious golf course. [LINK: ([448]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-448]  It was reported on November 7, 2014, that Timberlake had sold Mirimichi to Three Star Leasing LLC for $500,000. [LINK: ([449]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-449]  In October 2018, Timberlake and  [LINK: (Levi's) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Levi%27s]  debuted their collaborative clothing line collection "Fresh Leaves". [LINK: ([450]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-450]  In 2022, Justin Timberlake invested in Greenville, South Carolina par-3 golf course Greenville 3's. [LINK: ([451]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-451]

Timberlake provides celebrity endorsement for many commercial products, this aspect of his business being managed by  [LINK: (IMG) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IMG_(company)]  since April 2008. [LINK: ([452]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-452]  Major endorsements in 2009 included  [LINK: (Sony) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sony]  electronic products, [LINK: ([453]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-453]   [LINK: (Givenchy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Givenchy] 's men's fragrance " [LINK: (Play) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parfums_Givenchy#Fragrances_for_men] ", [LINK: ([454]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-454]  the  [LINK: (Audi A1) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Audi_A1] , [LINK: ([455]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-455]   [LINK: (Callaway Golf Company) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Callaway_Golf_Company]  products, [LINK: ([456]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-456]  [LINK: ([457]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-457]  and in 2011,  [LINK: (Myspace) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myspace] . [LINK: ([458]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-458]  [LINK: ([459]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-459]  In 2011, he teamed up with  [LINK: (Capital One) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capital_One]  to announce the winners of the inaugural Capital One Cup, in a six-minute advert, where he is repeatedly getting hit in the groin. [LINK: ([460]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-460]  In 2012, he hosted  [LINK: (Walmart) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walmart] 's annual shareholders meeting, [LINK: ([461]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-461]  saying, "I buy a lot at Walmart." [LINK: ([462]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-462]

In 2014, Timberlake partnered with  [LINK: (Sauza Tequila) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sauza_Tequila]  to re-launch his own version of the beverage as part of the Sauza franchise: Sauza 901. [LINK: ([463]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-463]  In 2016, he became an investor in the beverage company  [LINK: (Bai Brands) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bai_Brands] . [LINK: ([464]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-464]  In 2017,  [LINK: (Tiger Woods) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiger_Woods]  and Timberlake acquired an ownership stake in the Hurricane Junior Golf Tour. [LINK: ([465]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-465]

Timberlake and his wife Jessica Biel are minority owners of the  [LINK: (Memphis Grizzlies) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memphis_Grizzlies] . [LINK: ([466]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-466]  [LINK: ([467]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-467]

Timberlake is an  [LINK: (Air Jordan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Air_Jordan]  brand ambassador. His first collection with the brand, the Legend of the Summer collection, debuted on the co-headlining  [LINK: (tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Legends_of_the_Summer_Stadium_Tour]  of the same name with Jay-Z. These sneakers have gone on to resell for upwards of $10,000. [LINK: ([468]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-468]  In the lead up to his 2018 Super Bowl Halftime Show, Timberlake worked with famed  [LINK: (Nike, Inc.) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nike,_Inc.]  designer  [LINK: (Tinker Hatfield) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tinker_Hatfield]  to design his own version of the Air Jordan 3. [LINK: ([469]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-469]  Timberlake debuted the shoe at the halftime show. Timberlake's performance was estimated to be worth $2.86 million in marketing for Nike, and is credited for reigniting interested in the Nike and Air Jordan brand. [LINK: ([470]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-470]  [LINK: ([471]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-471]  Nike went on to release several colorways as part of the collaboration with Timberlake. [LINK: ([472]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-472]  [LINK: ([473]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-473]

In May 2022, Timberlake sold the rights to his entire musical catalog, around 200 songs he wrote or co-wrote, to  [LINK: (Hipgnosis) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hipgnosis_Songs_Fund]  Song Management for $100 million. The deal covers only pre-existing work, and not work he produces after the deal. [LINK: ([474]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-474]  [LINK: ([475]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-475]

Timberlake had an estimated net-worth of $250 million prior to the Hipgnosis deal, and is now estimated to be worth in excess of $350 million – making him one of the music industry's wealthiest solo performers. [LINK: ([476]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-476]

Timberlake has been active in several charitable pursuits, initially through NSYNC's "Challenge for the Children" aimed at a range of charities, and since 2001 through his "Justin Timberlake Foundation", which initially funded music education programs in schools, but now has a much broader agenda. [LINK: ([477]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-477]  In October 2005, the Grammy Association presented Timberlake with an award for his humanitarian efforts in Tennessee, alongside writer/director  [LINK: (Craig Brewer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Craig_Brewer] , also a Memphis native. [LINK: ([478]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-478]

In November 2007, he donated $100,000 from takings from his Australian tour to  [LINK: (Wildlife Warriors) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wildlife_Warriors]  founded by  [LINK: (Steve Irwin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steve_Irwin] . [LINK: ([479]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-479]  On March 23, 2008, he donated $100,000 to the  [LINK: (Memphis Rock N' Soul Museum) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memphis_Rock_N%27_Soul_Museum]  and another $100,000 to the Memphis Music Foundation. [LINK: ([480]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-480]

On November 12, 2007, the  [LINK: (PGA Tour) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PGA_Tour]  announced that Timberlake, an avid golfer who plays to a six  [LINK: (handicap) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Handicap_(golf)] , [LINK: ([481]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-481]  would become the host of the tour's  [LINK: (Las Vegas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Las_Vegas]  tournament starting in 2008. With Timberlake's agreement to host the tournament, its name was changed to the  [LINK: (Justin Timberlake Shriners Hospitals for Children Open) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake_Shriners_Hospitals_for_Children_Open] . He played in the celebrity pro-am on the day before the competitive tournament and hosted a charity concert during the week of the tournament. [LINK: ([482]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-482]  The activity was a success and was repeated in 2009. A review of the value of celebrities to fundraising concluded that Timberlake's contribution to Shriners Hospitals for Children was the single most valuable celebrity endorsement in the U.S. during 2009, and worth over $US9 million. [LINK: ([483]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-483]  However, in 2012, the event's chair Raoul Frevel told reporters Timberlake would no longer be involved in the event: "We tried everything we could to get him more involved with our kids and the hospitals. But it seemed that when the TV cameras weren't on, he disappeared." [LINK: ([484]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-484]

Timberlake often participates in the  [LINK: (American Century Championship) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Century_Championship]  [LINK: ([485]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-485]  and the  [LINK: (AT&T Pebble Beach Pro-Am) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AT%26T_Pebble_Beach_Pro-Am] . [LINK: ([486]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-486]  Both annual tournaments raise money for a range of national and local non-profits. [LINK: ([487]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-487]  [LINK: ([488]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-488]

In late 2012, Timberlake and his wife Jessica Biel volunteered in Far Rockaway, Queens over the weekend after  [LINK: (Hurricane Sandy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hurricane_Sandy] . Joined by their friend Timbaland, the couple helped distribute backpacks of supplies to members of the community who were still struggling after the hurricane. [LINK: ([489]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-489]

Timberlake has donated items for auction for several charities, including by  [LINK: (Ten O'Clock Classics) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ten_O%27Clock_Classics]  [LINK: ([490]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-490]  and  [LINK: (MusiCares) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MusiCares] . [LINK: ([491]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-491]  In 2010, Timberlake participated in the  [LINK: (Hope for Haiti Now) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hope_for_Haiti_Now]  telethon performing " [LINK: (Hallelujah) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hallelujah_(Leonard_Cohen_song)] ". The cover was made available for digital download with all proceeds donated to organizations doing relief work in Haiti. [LINK: ([492]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-492]  In 2016, Timberlake was featured in a new version of " [LINK: (Where Is the Love?) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Where_Is_the_Love%3F] ". The proceeds of the charity single will go to educational programs. [LINK: ([493]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-493]  In 2017, Timberlake and  [LINK: (Eminem) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eminem]  helped raise over $2 million for  [LINK: (Manchester Arena bombing) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manchester_Arena_bombing]  victims. [LINK: ([494]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-494]

Timberlake's autobiography,  [LINK: (Hindsight & All the Things I Can't See In Front of Me) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hindsight_(book)] , [LINK: ([495]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-495]  was released on October 30, 2018. [LINK: ([496]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-ew1-496]  The book covers some on and off camera candid images, the singer's early life and inspiration for songs. According to publisher HarperCollins, Hindsight includes a "collection of anecdotes, reflections, and observations on his life and work". [LINK: ([496]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Timberlake#cite_note-ew1-496]


